<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes)" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-3> ;
    schema:about "Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Fifth-order resolution of the odd-branch hexagon/triangle degeneracy (Bressloff 2001 Section 5.2), the full cubic coefficients with firing-rate derivative weights and quadratic feedback (Eq. 5.15), a Floquet solver or validated reproduction of Rule (2011) Fig. 8 (the vendored fixture is marked diagnostic-only upstream and the script says so), derivation of contoured vs non-contoured from the critical local harmonic (contour_mode is a preset flag), or a comparison with subject drawings of hallucinations",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling, even/odd orientation eigenbranches and marginal-stability scans, cubic amplitude-equation coefficients gamma_0, gamma_3(theta), eta_hex with unrestricted branch selection (rhombic angle = argmin gamma_3) and per-panel SELECTED / STABLE-coexisting / IMPOSED-unstable badges, the exact two-regime retino-cortical map with analytic inverse in a full-field theta in (-pi, pi] convention (bilateral-mirror mode kept and compared, seam contrast and mirror symmetry quantified), an orientation field drawn as line elements in cortex and in the visual field via the tangent map phi_R = phi + theta_R, rendered wavenumber |k| = q*/d_hyp quantised to integer torus cycles, exact parity with all 5 stability_reports and all 24 preset runs of the upstream fixture with all 133 of its paper-expectation checks counted (121 pass), a comparison of the map's magnification with Horton & Hoyt (1991) and with the 2002 paper's own scale anchors, parameter sweeps over lateral width, lateral inhibition and lateral spread (CLI --sweep), a Gaussian-only negative control cross-referenced to the vendored registry, and a diagnostic overlay of the Rule (2011) tongue boundaries (16 curves over 5 forcing amplitudes) vendored from the upstream MesmerPrism fixture with its calibration status printed",
        "reported_in_source: Bressloff et al. (2001, 2002): a Euclidean shift-twist symmetric neural field on the orientation-hypercolumn lattice of V1 undergoes a Turing-type instability whose even (contoured) and odd (non-contoured) planforms, pulled back through the retino-cortical map x=(alpha/eps)ln(1+eps r/w0), y=beta r theta/(w0+eps r), give Klüver's four form constants; the 2002 paper states a foveal magnification of 11.5 mm/deg, 30-36 perceived stripes and a cortical wavelength of 2.4-3.2 mm",
        "reported_in_source: Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): cortical rolls map to tunnels, funnels and spirals under the log-polar retino-cortical map",
        "reported_in_source: Horton & Hoyt (1991): human V1 linear cortical magnification follows M(E) = 17.3/(E + 0.75) mm/deg",
        "reported_in_source: Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011): periodic flicker drives 1:1 (stripe) and 2:1 period-doubling (hexagon) Floquet resonance tongues over forcing period and wave number",
        "reported_in_source: Tamekue, Prandi & Chitour (2024): a Gaussian-only (no Mexican-hat) lateral kernel produces no MacKay-type pattern, used here as the negative control",
        "transfer_boundary: Numerical parity to 2.2e-16 is with the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation's stability_reports and runs, not with digitised figures of the 2001 paper; alpha = 3/pi and beta = 1.589/2 are the upstream params.rs values (foveal magnification 10.98 vs the paper's 11.5 mm/deg) and the rendered cortical wavelength 8.7 mm is 3.1x the paper's 2.4-3.2 mm — both are computed and printed, not corrected",
        "transfer_boundary: Of the five gallery panels only the rhombic lattice is SELECTED by the cubic amplitude equations; the honeycomb is STABLE-coexisting and tunnel/spiral/cobweb are IMPOSED-unstable, because the bare orientation-overlap cubic coefficients make 2 gamma_3(theta*) < gamma_0 for every parameter value swept (rolls and squares never stable)",
        "transfer_boundary: The full-field pullback carries a discontinuity on the left horizontal meridian (seam contrast 7-10x for oblique modes) because the theta in (-pi, pi] branch cut maps to a line in cortex; the bilateral-mirror alternative removes the seam but destroys spiral chirality (mirror symmetry 1.000)" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1137/23M1616686>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-10>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-11>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-12>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-13>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v3-bressloff-v1-form-constants-9> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking Neural-Field Bifurcation & Log-Polar Retino-Cortical Geometry" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 6.77e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis (Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica)",
        "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis faithfully reproduces Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cervera-levin-mafe-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cervera-levin-mafe-2> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 55.6/100, audit 2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    schema:about "Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Exact equation-by-equation identity with the paywalled Cervera et al. (2021) full text or continuous 2D/3D biomechanical tissue deformation",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 1D AP (m1, m2) and ML (m3) reaction-diffusion analogue coupled with a 5-node bistable V_mem circuit port from MesmerPrism/rusty-matter and PlanformDB 2.5.0 canonical silhouettes",
        "reported_in_source: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021) model intercellular gap-junction blockade via effective diffusion reduction across AP (f2) and ML (f3) morphogen signals",
        "reported_in_source: Oviedo et al. (2010) and Durant et al. (2019) report crop-position-dependent double-head frequencies under octanol and triple-innexin RNAi and permanent two-headed regeneration after transient bioelectric depolarization",
        "transfer_boundary: One-parameter octanol crop-gradient calibration transferred to held-out triple-innexin RNAi crop frequencies" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py; output: cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif; organism: Planarians; photograph is Schmidtea mediterranea, empirical PlanformDB subset is Dugesia japonica; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/a0d6848; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, scipy 1.16.3, scikit-image 0.26.0; spec_fingerprint: ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc; artifact_sha256: 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/planform/planform_canonical_silhouettes_v1.json=cac26e64a315ed81...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-17-cervera-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021) model intercellular gap-junction blockade via effective diffusion reduction across AP (f2) and ML (f3) morphogen signals | Oviedo et al. (2010) and Durant et al. (2019) report crop-position-dependent double-head frequencies under octanol and triple-innexin RNAi and permanent two-headed regeneration after transient bioelectric depolarization; reconstructed_in_script: 1D AP (m1, m2) and ML (m3) reaction-diffusion analogue coupled with a 5-node bistable V_mem circuit port from MesmerPrism/rusty-matter and PlanformDB 2.5.0 canonical silhouettes; transfer_boundary: One-parameter octanol crop-gradient calibration transferred to held-out triple-innexin RNAi crop frequencies; does_not_claim: Exact equation-by-equation identity with the paywalled Cervera et al. (2021) full text or continuous 2D/3D biomechanical tissue deformation]; other sources: Smediterranea.jpg, from A Low Percent Ethanol Method for Immobilizing Planarians <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Smediterranea.jpg>, MesmerPrism/rusty-matter planarian bioelectric circuit and fixtures <https://github.com/MesmerPrism/rusty-matter/tree/ad111fa7ecfd8f43d292ff3b1d27d3af2741d828>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bioelechem.2019.107410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biosystems.2021.104511>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpj.2019.01.029>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.12.012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btt088> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-9> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Bioelectric Gap-Junction Coupled Nonlinear Dynamical Network" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 5.56e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-chindapol-coral-flow> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Chindapol flow-driven coral growth (Scleractinian coral Pocillopora verrucosa)",
        "Chindapol flow-driven coral growth faithfully reproduces Scleractinian coral Pocillopora verrucosa morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/chindapol-coral-flow-1> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Scleractinian coral Pocillopora verrucosa specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 55.5/100, audit 2026-10-13-morphology-audit) and the assessments." ;
    schema:about "Scleractinian coral Pocillopora verrucosa" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f3fe478/2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py; output: chindapol_coral_flow_morphospace.png; organism: Scleractinian coral Pocillopora verrucosa; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/f3fe478; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, scikit-image 0.26.0" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002849> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-13-morphology-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-13-morphology-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-13-morphology-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-13-morphology-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-13-morphology-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-13-morphology-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-13-morphology-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-13-morphology-audit-chindapol-coral-flow-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Advection-Diffusion Nutrient Transport & Péclet-Number Accretion" ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 5.55e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells> a pk:Claim ;
