<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace (Coiled molluscs in general; the six panels are labelled cf. Nautilus, Turritella, an ammonite, Conus, Cerithium, Helix (resemblance, not specimens))",
        "Raup shell coiling morphospace faithfully reproduces Coiled molluscs in general; the six panels are labelled cf. Nautilus, Turritella, an ammonite, Conus, Cerithium, Helix (resemblance, not specimens) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/raup-shell-coiling-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/raup-shell-coiling-2> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) create_raup_animations.py, 1966-raup.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Coiled molluscs in general; the six panels are labelled cf. Nautilus, Turritella, an ammonite, Conus, Cerithium, Helix (resemblance, not specimens) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 64.1/100, audit 2026-10-17-raup-audit) and the assessments." ;
    schema:about "Coiled molluscs in general; the six panels are labelled cf. Nautilus, Turritella, an ammonite, Conus, Cerithium, Helix (resemblance, not specimens)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Direct morphometric measurement of physical museum shell specimens or micro-CT meshes",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Parametric 3D surface generator raup_shell(W, D, T, S) with exact inverse parameter recovery recover_parameters() to < 1e-14 error across a 3x3x4 morphospace grid",
        "reported_in_source: Raup (1966), Noshita (2014), and Okabe & Yoshimura (2017) define logarithmic helicospiral shell coiling via whorl expansion W, radial distance D = r_min/r_max, translation T = dz_c/dr_c, and aperture shape S",
        "transfer_boundary: Six illustrative parameter sets in datasets/raup/variables.json labelled cf. canonical shell forms (planispiral, turreted, evolute disc, obconical, high-spired, globose)" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/1966-raup.py; output: raup_shell_animation.gif; organism: Coiled molluscs in general; the six panels are labelled cf. Nautilus, Turritella, an ammonite, Conus, Cerithium, Helix (resemblance, not specimens); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/ba6fd20; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: 99d02b160418b61e3ca5605bf1327defebc58c14533242de5ba9809a805bf905; artifact_sha256: 986555a0032be189233cbf0ec15193959bf7f9cc0b1e099a6b7a289f7cff8b02; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/raup/variables.json=c9c9cfaf70faa9a5...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-13-morphology-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Raup (1966), Noshita (2014), and Okabe & Yoshimura (2017) define logarithmic helicospiral shell coiling via whorl expansion W, radial distance D = r_min/r_max, translation T = dz_c/dr_c, and aperture shape S; reconstructed_in_script: Parametric 3D surface generator raup_shell(W, D, T, S) with exact inverse parameter recovery recover_parameters() to < 1e-14 error across a 3x3x4 morphospace grid; transfer_boundary: Six illustrative parameter sets in datasets/raup/variables.json labelled cf. canonical shell forms (planispiral, turreted, evolute disc, obconical, high-spired, globose); does_not_claim: Direct morphometric measurement of physical museum shell specimens or micro-CT meshes]; other sources: Geometric analysis of shell coiling: coiling in ammonoids <https://pubs.geoscienceworld.org/jpaleontol/article-abstract/41/1/43/80199/geometric-analysis-of-shell-coiling-coiling-in>" ;
