<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation (Conus textile Linnaeus, 1758 (textile cone snail))",
        "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation faithfully reproduces Conus textile Linnaeus, 1758 (textile cone snail) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py, docs/media/conus_textile_rule30.gif, docs/media/conus_rule30_kymograph_defect_fronts.png, conus_textile_rule30_metrics.csv, conus_rule30_defect_fronts.csv implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Conus textile Linnaeus, 1758 (textile cone snail) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 87.3/100, audit 2026-10-18-conus-audit) and the assessments." ;
    schema:about "Conus textile Linnaeus, 1758 (textile cone snail)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Infinite-horizon proof of the open 2019 Wolfram Rule 30 Prize Problems #1-#3 (verifies finite-horizon statistics through t = 1024 and exact diagonal periods through k = 414)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Exact Boolean and GF(2) ANF Rule 30 evolution, 1024-step single-seed light-cone, Jen (1990) left-bijective reconstruction and k=0..414 diagonal period-doubling cascade (k = 0, 3, 8, 29, 400), directional Boolean damage-cone ensemble, Meinhardt-Klingler PDE kymograph and lesion scar simulation, and 3D Raup Conus shell projection validated against segmented OSU Conus textile photography",
        "reported_in_source: Jen (1990) proves left-bijective spatial invertibility a_{t,i-1} = a_{t+1,i} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1}) and the left-cone diagonal period-doubling cascade d_k(t+1) = d_{k-2}(t) XOR (d_{k-1}(t) OR d_k(t)) gated by all-zero synchronizing barriers d_{k-1} = 0",
        "reported_in_source: Meinhardt & Klingler (1987) formulate a 1D mantle-edge activator-substrate-hormone reaction-diffusion PDE generating self-extinguishing pigment triangles and V-shaped lesion recovery wakes",
        "reported_in_source: Wolfram (1983, 1984, 2002) introduces elementary cellular automaton Rule 30 (a_{t+1,i} = a_{t,i-1} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1})) as a discrete generative model of Conus textile tent pigmentation and poses the 2019 Rule 30 Prize Problems on the center column a_{t,0} (OEIS A051023)",
        "transfer_boundary: Cross-model 1D space-time defect-front kymograph comparison linking Rule 30 / Meinhardt mantle wakes to Zhang-Goldstein-Levin (2025) frozen-defect cell sorting and Cervera-Levin-Mafe (2021) bioelectric domain-wall propagation" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/docs/media/conus_textile_rule30.gif, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/docs/media/conus_rule30_kymograph_defect_fronts.png, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/conus_textile_rule30_metrics.csv, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/conus_rule30_defect_fronts.csv; output: conus_textile_rule30_comparison.png; organism: Conus textile Linnaeus, 1758 (textile cone snail); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/fb234bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313; artifact_sha256: b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/conus/conus_textile_reference.json=dfcb500d87a39390...}; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Wolfram (1983, 1984, 2002) introduces elementary cellular automaton Rule 30 (a_{t+1,i} = a_{t,i-1} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1})) as a discrete generative model of Conus textile tent pigmentation and poses the 2019 Rule 30 Prize Problems on the center column a_{t,0} (OEIS A051023) | Jen (1990) proves left-bijective spatial invertibility a_{t,i-1} = a_{t+1,i} XOR (a_{t,i} OR a_{t,i+1}) and the left-cone diagonal period-doubling cascade d_k(t+1) = d_{k-2}(t) XOR (d_{k-1}(t) OR d_k(t)) gated by all-zero synchronizing barriers d_{k-1} = 0 | Meinhardt & Klingler (1987) formulate a 1D mantle-edge activator-substrate-hormone reaction-diffusion PDE generating self-extinguishing pigment triangles and V-shaped lesion recovery wakes; reconstructed_in_script: Exact Boolean and GF(2) ANF Rule 30 evolution, 1024-step single-seed light-cone, Jen (1990) left-bijective reconstruction and k=0..414 diagonal period-doubling cascade (k = 0, 3, 8, 29, 400), directional Boolean damage-cone ensemble, Meinhardt-Klingler PDE kymograph and lesion scar simulation, and 3D Raup Conus shell projection validated against segmented OSU Conus textile photography; transfer_boundary: Cross-model 1D space-time defect-front kymograph comparison linking Rule 30 / Meinhardt mantle wakes to Zhang-Goldstein-Levin (2025) frozen-defect cell sorting and Cervera-Levin-Mafe (2021) bioelectric domain-wall propagation; does_not_claim: Infinite-horizon proof of the open 2019 Wolfram Rule 30 Prize Problems #1-#3 (verifies finite-horizon statistics through t = 1024 and exact diagonal periods through k = 414)]; other sources: Geometric analysis of shell coiling: general problems <https://www.jstor.org/stable/1301992>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0167-2789(90)90169-P>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(87)80101-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/311419a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.55.601> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-conus-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-code-traceability>,
