<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-limbform-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — MorphoEval overall 71.3/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Decodes the Limbform formalism (segments as graph edges with length and direction, joints as vertices with border radii, sub-joints for grafts, digits with phalanx counts) for 555 of the 565 morphology rows of LimbformDB 2.1.0 — the other 10 are outcome labels without geometry — and draws each limb as a smooth outline through the joint control points with the paper's proximodistal red-to-blue gradient, green coxa, yellow basis/trochanter, black long bones and blue digits. Against the paper's own cartoons of the five Fig. 1 wild types the decoded silhouettes have the same topology, pose and segment/digit counts; bounding-box-aligned IoU is 0.41-0.74 (best for the cricket leg, worst for the frog hindlimb, where the thigh-shank angle differs). The joint-radius rule of the formalism holds for 3137 of 3146 joints when a sub-joint counts its host segment twice. Overall 71.3/100 (faithfulness 70.0, reproducibility 74.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 747c57f; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 85, Morphological realism / specimen match 65, Parameter expressivity 75, Morphometric validation 55, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 65. Output judged: limbform_wildtype_gallery.png: rendered output of 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py at 747c57f, image/png, 620043 B, 2400×1875 px, sha256 d561f4aab10756976c3fd5caf7a8c516da13c1cd9395d6cb5a54b8a2f5b10236." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Ask the Lobo lab for the LimbformDB licence so the file can be vendored with its hash.",
        "remediation needed: Compare at least the five wild types with photographs of the real limbs (Fig. 1 A-E), e.g. segment-length ratios, not only with the paper's cartoons.",
        "remediation needed: Confirm the Ang convention and the joint-radius order against the Limbform software source or the authors, and explain the Fig. 1 B''/C'' silhouette residuals.",
        "remediation needed: Pin the Python 3.14 environment (exact versions) in requirements or a lock file." ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.13e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-limbform-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Parameter expressivity: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Every encoded number has a visible effect: each radius moves one control point of the outline, each segment's Dist/Ang moves its distal joint and everything beyond it, each sub-joint places a graft, each digit's Dist/Ang/NumBones draws one digit. Morphologies in one frame share one scale, so size differences between phenotypes are preserved. There is no parameter sweep in the output and Side/Reversed/Inverted are only reported (no 2.1.0 entry uses them), so their effect is untested. Evidence: 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L286–L312: layout(): joint positions from Dist/Ang <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L286-L312>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L377–L400: build_geometry(): control points, pieces, digits <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L377-L400>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L788–L862: render_timeline(): shared scale per frame; category grids <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L788-L862>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-limbform-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Reproducibility package: 65/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Deterministic (no random state), invocation documented in the docstring and README, the input is fetched and hash-verified by the script itself, rows without geometry are skipped with a message, outputs are identical on re-run. Dependencies are in requirements.txt with lower bounds only and the known-good environment (Python 3.14) is recorded only in this audit. Evidence: 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L49–L60: documented invocation and outputs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L49-L60>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L885–L921: main(): download, checks, outputs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L885-L921>; requirements.txt L1–L7: lower bounds only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/requirements.txt#L1-L7>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-limbform-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Source and data traceability: 85/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Both papers are cited with DOIs, the database version, download URL, byte size and SHA-256 are recorded and verified on every run, the schema tables used are listed, and the reference figure used by the measurements is pinned by hash. The database's licence is not stated on the Lobo-lab page or in the file, which is why it is cached rather than vendored; that gap is the source's, but it is recorded here. Evidence: 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L14–L24: references with DOIs and database URL <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L14-L24>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L89–L93: URL, SHA-256 and size of the database <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L89-L93>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L200–L219: resolve_db_path(): download and hash check <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L200-L219>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L263–L284: load_first_report_year(): the join to Publication.Year <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L263-L284>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-limbform-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Morphological realism / specimen match: 65/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The only published renderings of these database entries are the cartoons in Fig. 1 of the Regeneration paper; side by side, the decoded axolotl forelimb, Xenopus hindlimb, fiddler-crab walking leg, cricket T3 leg and huntsman-spider leg have the same segments, digits, pose and colour scheme (gradient, coxa green, basis yellow, bones, digits). Measured on the figure, bounding-box-aligned silhouette IoU is 0.64, 0.41, 0.43, 0.74 and 0.49 for panels A''-E'': the cricket leg is essentially identical, the others differ in joint angles and segment width (the frog thigh-shank angle most of all), which may reflect a database revision after the figure was drawn or an angle convention not captured. Distinct morphologies (double limbs, grafts, branched chelipeds, missing segments) render distinctly. No photographs of real limbs are compared. Evidence: limbform_wildtype_gallery.png (generated output, not in repo): the five Fig. 1 wild types plus ten further wild-type limbs — limbform_wildtype_gallery.png: rendered output of 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py at 747c57f, image/png, 620043 B, 2400×1875 px, sha256 d561f4aab10756976c3fd5caf7a8c516da13c1cd9395d6cb5a54b8a2f5b10236; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L419–L453: boundary_tour(): Euler tour of the limb tree -> closed outline <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L419-L453>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L632–L666: colour_field(): the paper's gradient and flat colours <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L632-L666>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L678–L704: draw_bones(): long bones for salamanders and frogs only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L678-L704>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Code-to-model traceability: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The decoding rule, the coordinate convention (+y anterior, wild-type head->trunk angle 3pi/2) and the cartoon convention are documented where they are implemented, and region_outline() names the figure it reproduces. The radii-count rule was established by checking the database rather than quoted from a numbered equation, because the papers describe the formalism in prose. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L35–L38: coordinate convention <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L35-L38>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L321–L331: region_outline() docstring: arc construction and Fig. 1D <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L321-L331>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L211–L244: load_first_report_year(): experiment->publication join documented <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L211-L244>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Model fidelity to source: 85/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/planform-morphology-animation-1> ;
    rdfs:comment "Region shape parameters are interpreted with the formalism's own rule (0 links -> 4 radii right/anterior/left/posterior; 1 link -> +90/+180/+270 deg from the edge; k >= 2 links -> one radius per bisector of consecutive edges), region centres are placed from the RegionsLink Dist/Ang labels and borders at Ratio*Dist, and the rule is checked at load time against all 1181 regions in the database. The only element not taken from the source is how consecutive control radii are joined: a superellipse arc (n = 2.2 free, n = 7 at a border) chosen to reproduce Planform's Fig. 1D; the paper does not publish Planform's interpolant. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L20–L34: formalism as implemented, with the radii-count rule <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L20-L34>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L286–L314: control_points(): radii -> directions per link count <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L286-L314>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L248–L272: layout(): centres from Dist/Ang, borders from Ratio <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L248-L272>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L701–L715: check_encoding(): 1181/1181 regions obey the rule <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L701-L715>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L317–L355: superellipse interpolant between radii (not from the source) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L317-L355>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Morphometric validation: 45/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The script computes silhouette morphometrics (AP length, ML width, aspect, area, region and organ counts, length relative to wild type) for every morphology and can write them as CSV, and the measurements sidecar checks the decoded wild type against the radii encoded in the database (560 x 120 units). Nothing is yet compared with measurements of real animals or with values reported in the literature; the reference is the formalism, not a specimen. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L386–L412: morphometrics() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L386-L412>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L684–L698: write_csv() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L684-L698>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L713–L714: wild-type AP/ML printed at load <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L713-L714>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): wild-type silhouette AP length = 557.6 Planform units (reference 560, PlanformDB 2.5.0 RegionParam/RegionsLink of morphology 1 (80+200+200+80)) [union of decoded region outlines of Morphology 1, rasterised; bbox extent along the AP axis]; wild-type silhouette ML width = 119.8 Planform units (reference 120, trunk lateral radii 60+60) [as above, across the ML axis]; wild-type AP/ML aspect = 4.653 ratio (reference 4.667, encoded radii) [AP length / ML width of the decoded silhouette] — S. mediterranea in Lobo et al. 2013 Fig. 1A is of this order; the formalism, not a specimen, is the reference; morphologies rendered = 369 count [Morphology rows with at least one encoded region] — 372 rows in the database; 3 have no regions (Lethal, Midbody Buldge, Double head, side tail); distinct body silhouettes = 167 count (reference 369, upper bound: one silhouette per morphology) [unique (AP length, ML width, area to 100 units, #heads, #tails) tuples over all rendered morphologies] — 115 morphologies share the wild-type body and differ only in organs (ectopic eyes, doubled CNS, pharynx position, ...), which is how the database encodes them; distinct encodings (regions + links + organs) = 369 count (reference 369, every morphology row is a distinct phenotype) [unique tuples of every encoded number read from the database]; IoU wild type vs double head (#24) = 0.8884 ratio (reference < 1; the two bodies differ only at the posterior cap (tail -> second head), the rest of the difference is organs) [intersection-over-union of the two decoded silhouettes on a shared canvas (region centres aligned by layout)]; IoU wild type vs headless (#20) = 0.6116 ratio (reference ≈ (trunk+tail area)/(whole-body area) if the head is simply absent) [as above]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-8> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — MorphoEval overall 66.5/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Rewritten. The region graph of every PlanformDB morphology is now decoded exactly (polar radii per region, centres and borders from the RegionsLink labels, organs from the organ table) and drawn in Planform's own cartoon convention; wild type, double head, headless, cyclops and the other canonical phenotypes are visually distinct and recognisable as Planform drawings. Remaining gap: the formalism stores three radii per head, so species features such as auricles or a triangular head are not in the data and the renders still read as cartoons, not specimens. Overall 66.5/100 (faithfulness 66.1, reproducibility 67.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 161f269; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 85, Morphological realism / specimen match 60, Parameter expressivity 75, Morphometric validation 45, Source and data traceability 70, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 60. Output judged: planform_morphology_gallery.png: rendered output of 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py at 161f269, image/png, 443915 B, 1920×2160 px, sha256 77a7dfa087bf89441dc35c64bc0c96bccfdc15d44a3d600df766fb723a87ace5." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add per-species outline templates (auricles, head shape) layered on the decoded regions, clearly marked as not from the database.",
        "remediation needed: Compare the decoded aspect ratio and organ positions with measurements on photographed S. mediterranea / D. japonica.",
        "remediation needed: Pin dependency versions for the Python 3.14 environment used here.",
        "remediation needed: Record the sha256 and version of the PlanformDB file used, and its download location." ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.65e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Parameter expressivity: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Every encoded quantity now has a visible effect: each radius moves one control point of its region, each link moves a region centre and a border, each organ vector/rotation places one organ. All morphologies in a frame share one scale (frame_bounds), so the size and proportion differences between phenotypes are preserved. The final morphospace grid of the timeline fits each morphology to its cell, which deliberately trades scale for legibility. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L525–L531: frame_bounds(): common scale within a frame <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L525-L531>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L546–L565: render_gallery(): small multiples at common scale <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L546-L565>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L572–L681: render_timeline(): per-year pages, final grid fitted per cell <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L572-L681>; planform_morphospace_timeline.gif (generated output, not in repo): 68 frames: intro, 30 year pages, final morphospace grid of 359 dated morphologies — planform_morphospace_timeline.gif: rendered output of 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py at 161f269, image/gif, 3265519 B, 1500×780 px, 63 frames, sha256 f7c8cadf3c06c8351a49b6a47e1fc73fafafa7b430841771c14806fe54ce92a4." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Reproducibility package: 60/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Deterministic (no random state), invocation documented in the docstring and README, outputs reproduced identically on re-run, and morphologies with no encoded regions are skipped with a message rather than failing. Dependencies (numpy, scipy, matplotlib, Pillow) are in requirements.txt with lower bounds only, and the run depends on an unversioned external database. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L40–L43: documented invocation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L40-L43>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L196–L202: region-less morphologies skipped explicitly <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L196-L202>; requirements.txt L1–L7: lower-bound pins only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/requirements.txt#L1-L7>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Source and data traceability: 70/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Both source papers are cited with DOIs in the module docstring, the database version is named and the schema tables used are listed. The database itself is still an external file located through PLANFORM_DB_PATH; no hash or download URL is recorded, so the exact input cannot be verified from the repository alone. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L10–L16: DOIs of both Lobo et al. 2013 papers <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L10-L16>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L138–L146: resolve_db_path(): env var or CLI, no provenance recorded <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L138-L146>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Morphological realism / specimen match: 60/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Side by side with Planform's Fig. 1D (Biology Open) the wild type now has the same structure: a straight-sided body with flat head/trunk and trunk/tail borders, rounded caps, red head fading to pink, blue tail, oval eyes with pupils, green brain lobes and nerve cords, a tube pharynx. Double head (#24), headless (#20), cyclops, side heads and polarity-reversed morphologies are told apart at a glance; 167 distinct body silhouettes among 369 morphologies, the rest (115 of them wild-type bodied) differing only in organs, which is how the database encodes them. Against a photographed S. mediterranea the match is weaker: no auricles, no triangular head, no pigmentation; these are not encoded in the database. Evidence: planform_morphology_gallery.png (generated output, not in repo): 16 canonical phenotypes compared with Planform Fig. 1D and the Planform screenshots in Lobo et al. 2013 — planform_morphology_gallery.png: rendered output of 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py at 161f269, image/png, 443915 B, 1920×2160 px, sha256 77a7dfa087bf89441dc35c64bc0c96bccfdc15d44a3d600df766fb723a87ace5; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L78–L87: Planform colour convention <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L78-L87>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L460–L510: draw_morphology(): outline, gradient fills, organs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L460-L510>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Code-to-model traceability: 70/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Each analysis step names the source it follows and the decoding of the drawings is documented where it happens; the cell-length convention (maximum Feret diameter, cells bounded by vein mid-lines) was established by matching the authors' table rather than quoted from their methods text, which the script did not have access to. Evidence: 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L27–L35: what the re-segmentation does and why <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L27-L35>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L353–L364: docstring: mid-line convention and its effect <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L353-L364>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L383–L392: infer_scale(): calibration rules stated <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L383-L392>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Model fidelity to source: 70/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-1> ;
    rdfs:comment "The prediction under test is stated and operationalised exactly as it follows from the source model (constant cell size -> N ∝ L², median cell ∝ L⁰) and the measured quantity is the one Hoffmann et al. and Eshghi et al. both use (vein-bounded cell, length = maximum Feret diameter, verified by per-wing agreement with Table S1). The model itself is not run here (that is 2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py), and log-log OLS is the script's own choice of test, not the source's. Evidence: 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L36–L43: prediction derived from the source model <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L36-L43>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L137–L142: ols_loglog(): the test <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L137-L142>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L404–L413: cell_table(): cell length = max Feret diameter <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L404-L413>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Morphometric validation: 85/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "This is the script's strength. Cell count, median / mean / maximum cell length, cell area and circularity are re-measured on all 69 fossil drawings and compared wing by wing with the published Table S1 (median |ΔN|/N 0.0 %, median cell length 3.4 %, largest cell 0.9 %); extant counts are cross-checked against Hoffmann et al.'s independent segmentation of 42 shared species (median 3.1 %, r 0.992); disagreements are printed, not hidden (#7 drawing vs table row; #23/#24 swapped). The scale of each drawing is read from its own bar. Short of full marks because 4 of 69 drawings fall back to the tabulated wing length for calibration and the +3 % length bias is explained but not corrected. Evidence: 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L416–L446: resegment_fossils(): per-wing comparison table <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L416-L446>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L448–L483: report_resegmentation(): agreement statistics and flagged disagreements <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L448-L483>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L265–L349: read_scale_bar(): bar length and label read from the drawing <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L265-L349>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L935–L946: Hoffmann vs Eshghi count cross-check <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L935-L946>; datasets/odonata/fossil_wing_resegmentation.csv L1–L70: the 69 per-wing comparisons <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/datasets/odonata/fossil_wing_resegmentation.csv#L1-L70>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): cell count ∝ wing length^b, fossil = 1.7811 exponent (reference 2.0, isometric prediction for a constant cell size (Hoffmann et al. 2018 inhibition length)) [OLS slope of log10 cell count on log10 wing length, n=69 wings (Eshghi et al. 2026 tables)] — r = 0.739; median cell length ∝ wing length^b, fossil = -0.1673 exponent (reference 0.0, constant cell size) [OLS slope of log10 median cell length on log10 wing length]; median cell length over wings, fossil = 0.7837 mm [median over wings of the per-wing median cell length (Eshghi et al. 2026 tables)] — IQR 0.67–0.94 mm; cell count ∝ wing length^b, extant_dragonfly = 1.111 exponent (reference 2.0, isometric prediction for a constant cell size (Hoffmann et al. 2018 inhibition length)) [OLS slope of log10 cell count on log10 wing length, n=290 wings (Eshghi et al. 2026 tables)] — r = 0.816; median cell length ∝ wing length^b, extant_dragonfly = 0.2171 exponent (reference 0.0, constant cell size) [OLS slope of log10 median cell length on log10 wing length]; median cell length over wings, extant_dragonfly = 0.9885 mm [median over wings of the per-wing median cell length (Eshghi et al. 2026 tables)] — IQR 0.87–1.09 mm; cell count ∝ wing length^b, extant_damselfly = 1.0078 exponent (reference 2.0, isometric prediction for a constant cell size (Hoffmann et al. 2018 inhibition length)) [OLS slope of log10 cell count on log10 wing length, n=104 wings (Eshghi et al. 2026 tables)] — r = 0.872; median cell length ∝ wing length^b, extant_damselfly = 0.2765 exponent (reference 0.0, constant cell size) [OLS slope of log10 median cell length on log10 wing length]; median cell length over wings, extant_damselfly = 0.8991 mm [median over wings of the per-wing median cell length (Eshghi et al. 2026 tables)] — IQR 0.83–0.99 mm; fossil drawings re-segmented = 69 count (reference 69, fossil wings in Table S1) [fossil venation drawings in the Zenodo archive segmented by the script]; scale bar label read from the drawing = 65 count (reference 69) [drawings whose scale-bar label was read from the glyphs and found consistent with the tabulated wing length] — the rest use the bar with a value inferred from the tabulated wing length, or that length alone; cell count, median |ΔN|/N vs Table S1 = 0.0 ratio (reference 0.0, Eshghi et al. 2026 Table S1) [per-wing relative difference between the script's cell count and the published count, median over 69 wings] — 90% of wings within 2%; max 194% (#7, drawing and table row disagree); median cell length, median |Δ| vs Table S1 = 0.0339 ratio (reference 0.0, Eshghi et al. 2026 Table S1) [per-wing relative difference of the median cell length (maximum Feret diameter), median over wings] — signed mean +3.5% (cells bounded by vein mid-lines); largest cell length, median |Δ| vs Table S1 = 0.0094 ratio (reference 0.0, Eshghi et al. 2026 Table S1) [as above for the largest cell of each wing]; fossil median cell length, re-segmented = 0.8275 mm (reference 0.7837, same statistic from Table S1) [median over wings of the script's own per-wing median cell length]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-10>,
