        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-8>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-9> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — MorphoEval overall 76.0/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "A data comparison rather than a simulation: the one trait the Hoffmann venation model predicts (cell size set by an inhibition length) is compared on 69 fossil and 394 extant wings from Eshghi et al. 2026, with PBDB ages and Hoffmann et al.'s own segmentations as the extant counterpart. The fossil measurements are reproduced independently from the published drawings (cell counts to a median 0.0 %, median cell length to 3.4 %), which also exposes one table row that does not match its drawing and one swapped pair. Finding: median cell length stays at 0.78–0.99 mm across 150 Myr and a 6x range of wing length; the inhibition length is approximately, not strictly, conserved. Overall 76.0/100 (faithfulness 75.7, reproducibility 76.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit fbbcaf6; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, pandas 2.3.3, scikit-image 0.26.0, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 70, Morphological realism / specimen match 85, Parameter expressivity 50, Morphometric validation 85, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 70, Reproducibility package 70. Output judged: odonata_fossil_resegmentation.png: rendered output of 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py at fbbcaf6, image/png, 286190 B, 1663×1323 px, sha256 ab6f3b9f89fbcff0ff1fa942915cfcb3736ebde60723489a9ee8d7a39c8a5b38." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add scikit-image to requirements.txt and pin versions for the Python 3.14 environment.",
        "remediation needed: Correct the +3 % mid-line bias by eroding cells by half the measured vein width, or state the authors' convention once their methods text is available.",
        "remediation needed: Read the \"mm\" label with a proper template match so",
        "remediation needed: Report the discrepancies (#7," ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Parameter expressivity: 50/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "No generative parameters: the script analyses measured wings. The groups (fossil / dragonfly / damselfly) and the fitted exponents are outputs, not controls. Neutral score, not applicable. Evidence: 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L144–L173: report(): fits per group, nothing is tuned <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L144-L173>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "not applicable (neutral baseline)" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Reproducibility package: 70/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Deterministic, invocation documented with a no-download mode, inputs cached, resumed and hash-verified, every derived number written to CSV. Dependencies are lower-bound pins only and scikit-image, which the re-segmentation needs, is not in requirements.txt; the full run needs ~100 MB of downloads. Evidence: 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L45–L54: documented invocation and outputs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L45-L54>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L193–L227: fetch(): resumable, hash-checked <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L193-L227>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L80–L85: scikit-image optional import with explicit error <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L80-L85>; requirements.txt L1–L7: no scikit-image; lower bounds only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/requirements.txt#L1-L7>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Source and data traceability: 90/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Both papers carry DOIs, the data archive is a CC BY 4.0 Zenodo DOI, PBDB and GBIF query URLs and the retrieval date are recorded, the derived tables are vendored with a provenance README, and the two downloaded inputs are pinned by SHA-256 and verified on every run. Evidence: 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L12–L25: sources with DOIs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L12-L25>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L94–L101: URLs, byte size and SHA-256 of both downloads <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L94-L101>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L176–L191: verify_sha256() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L176-L191>; datasets/odonata/README.md L1–L20: provenance of every vendored column <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/datasets/odonata/README.md#L1-L20>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-odonata-audit-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata wing cells through deep time — Morphological realism / specimen match: 85/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Every image shown is a real specimen: the fossil venation drawings are rendered at true millimetre scale from their own scale bars and colour-coded by the re-measured cell length, the extant counterpart is Hoffmann et al.'s segmented Arigomphus / Aeshna wings, and the final animation frame places an Eocene and a living aeshnid at the same scale. The script's segmentation of the fossil drawings reproduces the authors' counts to a median 0.0 % (90 % of wings within 2 %). Not full marks because the extant wings are shown only as Hoffmann's domain boundaries, not photographs. Evidence: odonata_fossil_resegmentation.png (generated output, not in repo): four re-segmented fossil wings at one scale; scatter vs Table S1 — odonata_fossil_resegmentation.png: rendered output of 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py at fbbcaf6, image/png, 286190 B, 1663×1323 px, sha256 ab6f3b9f89fbcff0ff1fa942915cfcb3736ebde60723489a9ee8d7a39c8a5b38; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L352–L380: segment_fossil_cells(): skeletonised veins -> cells <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L352-L380>; 2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py L582–L596: show_wing_mm(): true-scale rendering <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L582-L596>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-celegans-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — Code-to-model traceability: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The docstring names the loader whose column semantics are followed, the ProductionInfo fields used, the source of every literature constant and the calibration reference; each check prints the value and the literature anchor it is compared with. The nuclei-file format itself (StarryNite/AceTree) is documented only by the WormGUIDES loader source, not by a paper section, so the trace stops at code rather than at a publication. Evidence: 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L1–L22: the four layers and what is decoded <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L1-L22>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L113–L124: LIT constants and the Sulston grammar <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L113-L124>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L266–L275: movie_offset(): the ProductionInfo field read <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L266-L275>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-celegans-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — Model fidelity to source: 80/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/santella-wormguides-celegans-1> ;
    rdfs:comment "Re-scored from 75. The atlas is decoded as the WormGUIDES application decodes it: the column positions follow AceTreeTableLineageDataLoader, the time offset and unit scale are read from ProductionInfo.csv, mesh cells and the eggshell outline are taken from CellShapesConfig.csv. The Sulston naming grammar and parent-of relation are implemented explicitly and tested on every name. The physical scale is now anchored to the atlas's own segmentation of the eggshell rather than to the nuclear cloud, so the one remaining assumption is that this egg has the typical 50 um length; the choice of the frame-330 shell over the static early mesh is justified in the code by the measured nuclear overrun. Not higher because that assumption remains, because the 3D atlas is shown as a 2D projection (back-to-front by z) rather than the application's 3D rendering, and because the connectome layer is a summed adjacency matrix that drops the chemical/electrical distinction and Cook et al.'s muscle and end-organ nodes. Evidence: 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L254–L275: read_nuclei()/movie_offset(): loader columns, ProductionInfo offset <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L254-L275>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L277–L319: founder()/parent_of()/check_encoding(): Sulston grammar and tree <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L277-L319>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L102–L113: WG_SHELL, SHELL_FRAMES, CALIB_FRAME, EMBRYO_LENGTH_UM <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L102-L113>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L335–L368: calibrate()/shell_report()/nuclear_cloud_scale(): the shell-based scale, why frame 330, the cross-check <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L335-L368>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L564–L595: canonical_cell()/draw_connectome(): neuron set and matrix <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L564-L595>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-celegans-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — Morphometric validation: 72/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Re-scored from 65. Per-frame morphometrics are computed and written to CSV (nucleus count by founder, extents, mean diameter, normalised E-cell radius) and compared in the script's own output against the literature: 113 deaths listed and all present, 562-571 nuclei at 330-350 min against ~550, 580 nuclei at the last frame against 558 at hatching (671 generated), E-cell ingression at 26 cells against the ~30-cell stage, and the 300 connectome neurons against 302. The calibration now has checks of its own: the fitted length leaves the shell width unfitted and it comes out 29.2 um against the ~30 um egg; the 13 sampled shell meshes bound the scale to 0.1649-0.1750 um per unit; the nuclear overrun of each shell mesh is measured (19.0 units for the static early mesh, 1.8 at frame 330); and the previous nuclear-cloud estimate is recomputed as a cross-check (2 % lower). The timing anchor still disagrees (movie-minute 73 against 100 min) and is reported as a discrepancy, not explained, and no nuclear-diameter reference is compared. Evidence: 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L348–L368: shell_report(): shell lengths, nuclear overrun, scale bracket <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L348-L368>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L370–L388: measure(): per-frame morphometrics <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L370-L388>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L401–L423: literature_checks(): the anchors printed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L401-L423>; morphoeval/measure_outputs.py L383–L468: measure_celegans(): the same values plus the four shell measurements in the sidecar <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/morphoeval/measure_outputs.py#L383-L468>; celegans_four_views.png (generated output, not in repo): the output judged — celegans_four_views.png: rendered output of 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py at 303a87e, image/png, 424197 B, 2240×1680 px, sha256 eb4b60086280c9a1740358c26fc655598f25d2adad63a9fcdb9c3a7980cc3bd6. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): lineage names parsing as Sulston names = 1330 count (reference 1330, all distinct names in the atlas) [distinct names in the 360 nuclei files matching ^(AB|MS|E|C|D|EMS|P[0-4]|Z[23])[aplrdv]*$]; cells first seen after their parent = 1326 count (reference 1326, all cells whose parent is in the movie (4 founders present at frame 1 have parents that predate it)) [non-founder cells whose parent name appears in an earlier frame]; calibration = 0.1649 µm per atlas unit [x extent of the atlas's eggshell outline mesh at frame 330 (obj_files/embryo_t330.obj, 'Embryo Outline' in CellShapesConfig.csv; 303.1 units) set to the 50 µm egg length] — assumption: Gönczy et al. 1999 JCB 144:927 ('50-µm-long cell'); the atlas coordinates are unit-less (ProductionInfo X/Y/Z_SCALE = 1); the earlier nuclear-cloud estimate gives 0.1617; the sampled shell meshes give 0.1649-0.1750; eggshell width under the calibration = 29.238 µm (reference 30.0, Gönczy et al. 1999 JCB 144:927 / WormAtlas: the egg is ~50 x 30 µm) [y extent of the eggshell outline mesh at frame 330 (z extent 28.9 µm)] — a consistency check of the calibration: the width is not fitted; eggshell length spread across sampled shell meshes = 17.3733 atlas units [max - min x extent of the eggshell meshes at frames [1, 30, 60, 100, 200, 250, 280, 300, 320, 330, 340, 350, 359] (285.8-303.1)] — one static mesh is reused for frames 1-~250, re-segmented per frame from ~280; the spread bounds the scale uncertainty (~6 %); nuclear overrun of the shell in x = 19.0129 atlas units [largest distance by which a nucleus (centroid ± radius) lies outside the shell mesh's x range at the sampled frames] — 1.8 units at frame 330; the overrun is against the static early mesh, which is why the calibration uses the re-segmented shell; nuclear cloud width at the last frame = 27.28 µm [y span of nuclear centroids + one mean diameter under the calibration] — nuclei do not reach the eggshell; compare the eggshell width above; nuclei at the last frame = 580 count (reference 558, WormAtlas, Embryo introduction (Sulston et al. 1983), accessed 2026-10-15: 558 cells at hatching (671 generated, 113 deaths)) [valid rows of t360-nuclei (movie-minute 379)] — the movie ends before hatching; 553 of the 580 nuclei carry a parts-list identity; maximum nucleus count = 585 count (reference 550, WormAtlas, Embryo introduction (Sulston et al. 1983), accessed 2026-10-15: ~550 cells at the end of proliferation (330-350 min)) [maximum over the 360 frames]; deaths listed by the atlas = 113 count (reference 113, WormAtlas, Embryo introduction (Sulston et al. 1983), accessed 2026-10-15: 113 embryonic cell deaths) [names in CellDeaths.csv]; listed dying cells that occur in the movie = 113 count (reference 113) [CellDeaths.csv names present in at least one nuclei file]; gastrulation onset, cell count = 26 count (reference 30, WormAtlas, Embryo introduction (Sulston et al. 1983), accessed 2026-10-15: ~30-cell stage (26-28 cells when Ea/Ep ingress)) [first frame from which the E cells sit at < 0.8 of the median normalised radius for 5 frames]; gastrulation onset, movie-minute = 73 min (reference 100, WormAtlas, Embryo introduction (Sulston et al. 1983), accessed 2026-10-15: Ea/Ep enter the embryo at 100 min after first cleavage) [same frame, frame index + movie start offset] — discrepancy: the atlas clock runs ~27 min ahead of the Sulston schedule at the same cell stage; not resolved by the script (temperature or time origin); nuclei at movie-minute 330-350 = 562-571 count (reference 550, WormAtlas, Embryo introduction (Sulston et al. 1983), accessed 2026-10-15: ~550 cells at 330-350 min) [nucleus count over that window]; neurons in the connectome edge list = 300 count (reference 302, Cook et al. 2019 / White et al. 1986: 302 hermaphrodite neurons) [upper-case node names of c302 herm_full_edgelist.csv after DA01->DA1 canonicalisation] — CANL/CANR are 'no synapses' in the WormGUIDES parts list and so cannot appear in an edge list." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-16-celegans-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-1>,
