<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-celegans-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — MorphoEval overall 70.2/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Downloads the WormGUIDES atlas at a pinned commit and verifies 429 files against a SHA-256 manifest; decodes the 360 StarryNite nuclei tables with the column semantics of the WormGUIDES loader (valid flag, x, y, z, diameter, lineage name) and the movie-start offset of ProductionInfo.csv; checks that all 1330 distinct names follow the Sulston grammar and that every cell whose parent is in the movie appears after it (1326/1326); re-derives the lineage chart from the names; sets the atlas's own eggshell outline mesh at frame 330 to the 50 um egg length (0.1649 um per unit; the shell's unfitted width comes out 29.2 um, the 13 sampled shell meshes bracket the scale at 0.1649-0.1750, the earlier nuclear-cloud estimate was 0.1617); draws the nuclei to scale inside the shell outline at six stages, 51 single-cell meshes at frame 330 and the c302 connectome adjacency matrix (300 neurons after name canonicalisation). Reports that the atlas reuses a static shell mesh for frames 1-~250 that the nuclei overrun by up to 19 units. Against WormAtlas's quotation of Sulston et al. the cell-stage anchors agree (113 listed deaths all present, 562-571 nuclei at 330-350 min against ~550, E-cell ingression at 26 cells against the ~30-cell stage) but the clock runs ~27 min ahead (gastrulation at movie-minute 73 against 100), which the script reports and does not resolve. Overall 70.2/100 (faithfulness 67.6, reproducibility 76.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 303a87e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 62, Parameter expressivity 50, Morphometric validation 72, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 70. Output judged: celegans_four_views.png: rendered output of 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py at 303a87e, image/png, 424197 B, 2240×1680 px, sha256 eb4b60086280c9a1740358c26fc655598f25d2adad63a9fcdb9c3a7980cc3bd6." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Draw the connectome with chemical and electrical edges separated, and keep the muscle/end-organ nodes that Cook et al. include.",
        "remediation needed: Pin the Python 3.14 environment (exact versions) in requirements or a lock file.",
        "remediation needed: Place a WormGUIDES figure panel (Santella et al. 2015 is CC BY) or a DIC frame beside the decoded nuclei at the same stage and measure the agreement.",
        "remediation needed: Replace the 50 um assumption with the acquisition voxel size of DISPIM_061416 (not in the repository's ProductionInfo.csv; ask the Bao lab), and ask why the shell mesh is static for frames 1-~250 while the nuclei overrun it.",
        "remediation needed: Resolve the ~27 min clock offset against Sulston's schedule (recording temperature, or the meaning of \"movie start time 20 min\") with the Bao lab or the diSPIM metadata." ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.02e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-celegans-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — Parameter expressivity: 50/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Not applicable: the script decodes a recorded atlas, it has no morphospace parameters. The only knobs are the calibration length, the frames shown and the gastrulation detector's threshold, all of which are constants stated in the code. Scored neutral so that it neither rewards nor penalises the overall. Evidence: 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L113–L122: EMBRYO_LENGTH_UM and the literature constants <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L113-L122>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L390–L398: gastrulation_onset(): threshold and hold <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L390-L398>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "not applicable (neutral baseline)" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-celegans-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — Reproducibility package: 70/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Deterministic, invocation documented in the docstring and README, the inputs are fetched and hash-verified by the script itself and missing mesh files are handled (the shape config's frame ranges are sparse), outputs are identical on re-run. First run needs network access to raw.githubusercontent.com; dependencies are in requirements.txt with lower bounds only, and the known-good environment is recorded only in this audit. Evidence: 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L32–L40: documented invocation and outputs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L32-L40>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L201–L227: _fetch(): download, sparse mesh handling <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L201-L227>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L674–L723: main() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L674-L723>; requirements.txt L1–L7: lower bounds only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/requirements.txt#L1-L7>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-celegans-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — Source and data traceability: 85/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Both repositories are pinned to a commit and licence, every input file has a SHA-256 in datasets/celegans/pinned_inputs.sha256 that is checked on every run, the papers are cited with DOIs, the acquisition metadata (image series, strain, frame interval, movie start) is read from the atlas's own ProductionInfo.csv, and the WormAtlas pages are cited with URL and access date. The Sulston counts and timings are quoted second-hand via WormAtlas rather than from the 1983 paper. Evidence: 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L24–L49: references, commits, licences, what each is used for <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L24-L49>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L92–L111: pinned commits and paths, including the shell meshes <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L92-L111>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L163–L199: fetch_inputs(): manifest verification <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L163-L199>; datasets/celegans/pinned_inputs.sha256 L1–L3: manifest header: commits and retrieval date <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/datasets/celegans/pinned_inputs.sha256#L1-L3>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-16-celegans-audit-santella-wormguides-celegans-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "WormGUIDES C. elegans embryo atlas with the OpenWorm connectome — Morphological realism / specimen match: 62/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Re-scored from 60. The re-derived lineage chart has the shape of Sulston's diagram (founder sub-trees in order, AB dominating, P4 ending in two cells); the nuclei are now drawn inside the atlas's eggshell outline, which fills the 50 x 29 um egg and shows the cloud growing out to the shell, and gastrulation shows as the E cells moving inward. Distinct stages are visually distinct. The gain is small because the shell is the atlas's segmentation, not a photograph: no DIC frame or WormGUIDES screenshot is placed beside the output, the WormAtlas images are only cited, and the meshes at frame 330 are drawn as flat projections, so resemblance to the real embryo is still argued from counts and extents rather than shown side by side. Evidence: celegans_four_views.png (generated output, not in repo): lineage chart, six stages inside the shell outline, meshes, connectome — celegans_four_views.png: rendered output of 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py at 303a87e, image/png, 424197 B, 2240×1680 px, sha256 eb4b60086280c9a1740358c26fc655598f25d2adad63a9fcdb9c3a7980cc3bd6; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L433–L480: lineage_layout()/draw_lineage(): the chart from the names <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L433-L480>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L482–L508: draw_shell()/draw_embryo(): shell hull, discs at recorded diameter, z-ordered <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L482-L508>; 2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py L520–L541: draw_meshes(): the atlas's OBJ shapes in the nuclei frame <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L520-L541>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-santella-wormguides-celegans-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Code-to-model traceability: 60/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The revision substantially improves internal traceability: model constants are centralized and disclaimed as local, f2 and f3 have one mapping each, fitting and held-out roles are explicit, every-sample parity is correctly scoped, and panel D admits its illustrative time rescaling. The phenotype number can be reconstructed from Planform geometry and renderer conventions. It is not, however, a source-derived biological criterion: the 100-unit pharynx length is a renderer constant, the denominator uses padded plotting bounds, and no paper supports the rule that passing this point creates a second head. Crop-specific circuit wound gains remain uncited, and the 2021 solver still cannot be traced to numbered source equations. Panel D's hard-coded legend values and pulse shading also disagree with current simulation output despite the improved title. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L27–L47: clear boundary between analogue, circuit port, criterion and silhouette measurement <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L27-L47>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L302–L338: centralized parameter mappings and reconstructible but uncited phenotype rule <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L302-L338>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L390–L415: silhouette extent used by the criterion contains 20-unit plotting padding <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L390-L415>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L526–L531: 100-unit pharynx length is a drawing convention, not an organ-table field <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L526-L531>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1262–L1305: time rescaling is acknowledged, but pulse span and legend percentages remain hard-coded and stale <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1262-L1305>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Model fidelity to source: 45/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cervera-levin-mafe-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cervera-levin-mafe-2> ;
    rdfs:comment "The program now accurately describes itself as a qualitative analogue built from the abstract and presentation, and explicitly disclaims equation, boundary-condition and parameter fidelity. Its high-level structure remains consistent with accessible source text: two antagonistic axial signals, an independent orthogonal signal and reduced effective diffusion under GJ block. f3 now genuinely changes D3 and an ML profile, replacing the false 2D heatmap with two honest independent curves. This still cannot score as a reproduction of the published model: the full 2021 paper was unavailable, the local solver docstring still says it implements the paper's system, no published equation or constants are verified, and m3 is not coupled to a morphological outcome. The rusty-matter port remains a separate unpublished educational model rather than the cited 2020 ion-channel model. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L27–L47: scope statement distinguishes qualitative analogue, educational port and measured silhouette <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L27-L47>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L213–L318: implemented AP and ML solvers, centralized constants and f2/f3 mappings <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L213-L318>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L230–L234: function docstring still attributes the unverified equations directly to Cervera 2021 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L230-L234>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1055–L1064: f3 now drives D3 and a nonconstant lateral index, explicitly independent of AP <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1055-L1064>; datasets/planform/README.md L21–L27: repository source boundary describes both mechanisms as qualitative or semi-quantitative abstractions <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/datasets/planform/README.md#L21-L27>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Morphometric validation: 48/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "This dimension has the clearest improvement. A one-parameter f2=1-a p model is fit to four octanol crop positions and evaluated, without refitting, against four innexin-RNAi positions; training RMSE is 4.2 points and held-out RMSE is 23.5 with r=0.94. The code reports these values in the figure and CSV, writes direct solver wavefronts, and measures anterior territory area on the photographic silhouette. This is a real model-data comparison rather than decorative anchors. It remains below the midpoint because four related positions are a very small validation set, no sampling uncertainty or baseline is reported, the 23.5-point held-out error is substantial, and the target is phenotype frequency while the predictor is a normalized signal-boundary index. The silhouette quantity is measured on a real body but is not compared with a measured treated specimen. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L997–L1018: one-parameter training and held-out evaluation, explicitly acknowledged as weak <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L997-L1018>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1048–L1053: direct x*, shift index and photographic-mask area are computed per crop <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1048-L1053>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1090–L1130: CSV contains direct wavefronts, fit metrics, f2 and f3 sweeps <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1090-L1130>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1207–L1259: panel C displays training and held-out metrics with empirical frequencies <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1207-L1259>; cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): regenerated table reports RMSE 4.2/23.5, r=0.94 and exact solver wavefronts — cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py at a0d6848, text/csv, 5146 B, artifact_sha256 36e3036d0379d9fcb3bd1b4c646d04092c959c5ed03387d4937d8ac7d461afee (sha256 36e3036d0379d9fcb3bd1b4c646d04092c959c5ed03387d4937d8ac7d461afee), spec_fingerprint ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): rusty-matter trace parity, max |Δ| = 0.0332 state units (reference 0.0, MesmerPrism/rusty-matter commit ad111fa7ecfd8f43d292ff3b1d27d3af2741d828) [maximum absolute difference across all 5 scenarios, 11 sampled steps and 4 state averages against rusty_matter_planarian_traces.json]; symmetric RD wavefront x*(f2=1) = 0.5 AP fraction (reference 0.5, symmetric boundary conditions at x=0 and x=L) [zero crossing of m1(x) - m2(x) when D2 = D2_0]; pharynx-boundary criterion x*_b = 0.5833 AP fraction [posterior end of the Planform #1 wild-type pharynx on the AP extent] — crossed at f2_b = 0.4197 (where x*(f2_b) = 0.5833); anterior body-area fraction on S. mediterranea silhouette (f2=1 -> f2=0.25) = 0.1561 fraction of body area [increase in real-silhouette mask area anterior to x*(f2) from f2=1.0 (0.483) to f2=0.25 (0.639)]; ML centre/edge ratio λ(f3), f3=1.0 vs f3=0.3 = 0.1855 ratio difference (reference >0 (monotonic decrease under lateral gap-junction blockade)) [m3(L_z/2)/m3(0) drop from f3=1.0 (0.197) to f3=0.3 (0.011)]; Oviedo 2010 octanol crop-gradient training RMSE = 4.1871 percentage points (reference 0.0, PlanformDB 2.5.0 / Oviedo et al. 2010 Dev. Biol. 339:188) [1-parameter fit f2(p) = 1 - 0.58*p against Oviedo et al. 2010 octanol double-head frequencies (Exps 415-418, n=4 crops)]; Oviedo 2010 triple-innexin RNAi held-out RMSE = 23.5215 percentage points (reference 0.0, PlanformDB 2.5.0 / Oviedo et al. 2010 Dev. Biol. 339:188) [held-out prediction error of the octanol-fitted curve against Dj-Inx-12 + Dj-Inx-5/13 RNAi double-head frequencies (Exps 446-449, n=4 crops)] — Pearson r = 0.943; circuit posterior head readout, memory ON vs memory OFF control = 0.9185 readout [0,1] (reference 0.23491399812436778, TransientDepolarizationNoMemoryControl negative control (Durant et al. 2019 Biophys. J. 116:948)) [final posterior head-identity readout R_head,post under TransientDepolarizationMemory] — hysteresis memory sustains depolarised head fate after transient pulse ends; Planform #1 Wild Type vs #2 Double Head silhouette IoU = 0.9478 ratio (reference <1.0 (posterior tail replaced by ectopic head cap), PlanformDB 2.5.0 morphologies #1 and #2) [256x256 shared-canvas intersection-over-union of decoded Lobo et al. (2013) graph silhouettes]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-morphometric-validation> ;
