        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-9> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — MorphoEval overall 55.6/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "A deterministic synthesis combines an explicitly labelled qualitative reaction–diffusion analogue, an orthogonal m3 profile, an educational rusty-matter circuit port, 14 curated PlanformDB records, a one-parameter crop-position fit and two fixed Planform cartoons. The additional outputs are cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png and cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv. The inert f3 and incorrect crop-wavefront defects are fixed, the silhouette is quantitatively sampled, and the empirical comparison now reports training and held-out errors. Remaining limits are the inaccessible full model papers, no f3-to-anatomy mapping, an uncited phenotype decision rule, weak held-out accuracy, fixed cartoon outcomes, illustrative time mapping and an incorrect reported f2 threshold caused by clipping in its inverse. Overall 55.6/100 (faithfulness 46.4, reproducibility 76.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit a0d6848; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0, scipy 1.16.3, scikit-image 0.26.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 45, Morphological realism / specimen match 42, Parameter expressivity 58, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 82, Code-to-model traceability 60, Reproducibility package 84. Output judged: cervera_levin_mafe_gj_block.gif: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted). Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc; artifact_sha256: 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/planform/planform_canonical_silhouettes_v1.json=cac26e64a315ed81...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-17-cervera-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021) model intercellular gap-junction blockade via effective diffusion reduction across AP (f2) and ML (f3) morphogen signals | Oviedo et al. (2010) and Durant et al. (2019) report crop-position-dependent double-head frequencies under octanol and triple-innexin RNAi and permanent two-headed regeneration after transient bioelectric depolarization; reconstructed_in_script: 1D AP (m1, m2) and ML (m3) reaction-diffusion analogue coupled with a 5-node bistable V_mem circuit port from MesmerPrism/rusty-matter and PlanformDB 2.5.0 canonical silhouettes; transfer_boundary: One-parameter octanol crop-gradient calibration transferred to held-out triple-innexin RNAi crop frequencies; does_not_claim: Exact equation-by-equation identity with the paywalled Cervera et al. (2021) full text or continuous 2D/3D biomechanical tissue deformation." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Calibrate or remove the illustrative 24-hour circuit overlay, generate legend values and pulse bounds from the simulation, and either source or remove the crop-specific rusty-matter wound-gain lookup.",
        "remediation needed: Fix f2_for_shift so it solves wavefront_for_f2(f2) = x_star_b without a clipped objective, test the recovered crossing, and correct the CSV/panel value from 0.20 to the actual approximately 0.42.",
        "remediation needed: Map f3 to a measured lateral morphology such as auricle width or head shape and compare it with specimens or source figures; otherwise describe f3 only as signal-profile expressivity.",
        "remediation needed: Obtain the full 2021 paper and map the analogue against its actual equations, boundary conditions, blocker factors and parameter definitions; retain the analogue label for every unmatched element.",
        "remediation needed: Replace the pharynx-crossing decision rule with a cited or empirically tested morphogen-to-phenotype mapping; if retaining this geometry, use actual body-mask bounds and state explicitly that the rule itself is an assumption.",
        "remediation needed: Validate the crop model on more independent experiments, include sampling uncertainty and simple baselines, and explain whether a 23.5-point held-out RMSE is adequate for the intended claim." ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.56e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Parameter expressivity: 58/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Both named reaction–diffusion factors now have visible monotonic effects across stated sweeps: decreasing f2 advances x* and the silhouette's anterior area share, while decreasing f3 sharply lowers the ML centre/edge concentration ratio. The self-test asserts both monotonic f2 response and a non-inert f3 range, and panel E shows the profiles rather than a misleading 2D surface. Credit is limited because f3 changes only an independently normalized concentration curve and is never translated into lateral head or auricle form; morphology remains a binary cartoon switch. The circuit's crop-specific wound gains also remain a fixed lookup rather than an independently tested parameterization. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L302–L318: single definitions of f2 wavefront and f3 centre/edge index <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L302-L318>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L965–L973: f2 sweep computes both wavefront and real-mask area share <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L965-L973>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1055–L1064: f3 sweep produces nonconstant ML profiles and lambda values <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1055-L1064>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1310–L1337: panel E visibly presents the two independent parameter curves <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1310-L1337>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1422–L1428: self-test checks f2 monotonicity and f3 sensitivity <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1422-L1428>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Reproducibility package: 84/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The environment exactly matched the recorded Python and five package versions, dependencies are locked, inputs are hash checked, and two complete runs produced byte-identical PNG, CSV and 46-frame GIF. The expanded self-test checks symmetry, f2 monotonicity, f3 sensitivity and every crop CSV wavefront, while port parity now compares all 11 frames and four state fields for every scenario and accurately says this is not biological validation. The package is held below a higher score because the test only checks that the fit metrics are finite, not correct; it misses the f2 inverse defect that prints 0.20 instead of the approximately 0.42 crossing; and it does not verify stale panel-D labels. The full prescribed repeat also took about 12.5 minutes, mostly because self-test renders the complete analysis figure. Evidence: requirements.lock.txt L18–L41: tested scientific dependencies are pinned <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/requirements.lock.txt#L18-L41>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L700–L770: hash verification and all-frame, all-field port parity <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L700-L770>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1412–L1442: expanded self-test, including CSV recomputation but no assertion of expected fit or inverse threshold <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1412-L1442>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L341–L351: clipped target inversion returns the lower bound for target=1 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L341-L351>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1537–L1587: headless-capable CLI and correctly scoped self-test output <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1537-L1587>; cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): regenerated byte-identically in two independent runs — cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py at a0d6848, image/png, 547708 B, 2330×1781 px, artifact_sha256 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77 (sha256 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77), spec_fingerprint ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc; cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): regenerated byte-identically with direct solver wavefronts — cervera_levin_mafe_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py at a0d6848, text/csv, 5146 B, artifact_sha256 36e3036d0379d9fcb3bd1b4c646d04092c959c5ed03387d4937d8ac7d461afee (sha256 36e3036d0379d9fcb3bd1b4c646d04092c959c5ed03387d4937d8ac7d461afee), spec_fingerprint ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Source and data traceability: 82/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Source and data traceability was already strong: papers have resolvable DOIs, rusty-matter is pinned to a full commit, fixtures and photograph have SHA-256 values, and PlanformDB-derived records retain experiment IDs and sample counts. The previously wrong 2021 PMID is corrected to 34411690, and the script now records exactly which source material was and was not consulted. It also labels fitted versus held-out empirical series. Remaining limits are that the full 2021 and 2020 papers were not accessible and the raw PlanformDB was not independently re-extracted, so the curated fixture transcription and equation provenance remain unverified. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L6–L47: correct PMID, source DOIs and explicit scope/source-access boundary <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L6-L47>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L98–L130: fixture and photograph hashes, URL, species and credit <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L98-L130>; datasets/planform/README.md L1–L19: PlanformDB pin, notice, upstream commit, fixture hashes and experiment groups <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/datasets/planform/README.md#L1-L19>; datasets/planform/rusty_matter_planformdb_derived_v0.json L1–L39: database identity, raw checksum, citations and selection policy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/datasets/planform/rusty_matter_planformdb_derived_v0.json#L1-L39>; datasets/planform/paper_citations.bib L29–L80: bibliographic records for model and empirical sources <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/datasets/planform/paper_citations.bib#L29-L80>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-cervera-audit-v2-cervera-levin-mafe-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera–Levin–Mafe gap-junction reaction–diffusion and bioelectric synthesis — Morphological realism / specimen match: 42/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The real Schmidtea silhouette is now used for an area measurement as well as a backdrop, and the regenerated figure is more legible than the previous version. Wild type and double head remain visibly distinct. But the body outline never changes, no real treated or double-head specimen or source-paper morphology is shown, and the model does not generate head or auricle form. Crossing a threshold merely swaps between two pre-existing Planform cartoons; measuring coloured territory area improves quantification, not anatomical realism. Thus the central specimen-match requirement remains mostly unmet. Evidence: 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L150–L207: photograph is segmented into the fixed mask on which signals are painted <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L150-L207>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L354–L362: new morphometric is the mask area lying anterior to the one-dimensional signal crossing <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L354-L362>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L795–L869: outcomes remain fixed WT and double-head Planform graph cartoons <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L795-L869>; 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py L1511–L1519: GIF threshold selects one of the two cartoons rather than deforming anatomy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L1511-L1519>; cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): regenerated six-panel figure is legible but contains no real phenotype comparison — cervera_levin_mafe_bioelectric_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py at a0d6848, image/png, 547708 B, 2330×1781 px, artifact_sha256 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77 (sha256 3f521835636f3530ddf73b0ea3142db13d605b319aac93fc940e3d8f07fc5f77), spec_fingerprint ca184becec2bf47d8a969d42711868cd85769dd013f7492905afdaf9707bf2fc." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gpt-5.6-sol> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-cervera-levin-mafe-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Code-to-model traceability: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The docstring maps each parameter to its definition and its line of code, the generating function is commented line by line with the identity each line enforces, the self-test names what it excludes, and the parameter sets carry a note on why each value. Not higher because the equations are tied to the secondary sources' notation rather than to numbered equations of Raup 1966. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L81–L107: raup_shell() docstring and comments <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L81-L107>; 1966-raup.py L1–L18: equations in the module docstring <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/1966-raup.py#L1-L18>; datasets/raup/README.md L32–L52: the model as a table: symbol, equation, meaning <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/datasets/raup/README.md#L32-L52>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Model fidelity to source: 80/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/raup-shell-coiling-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/raup-shell-coiling-2> ;
    rdfs:comment "The three parameters now mean what Raup's model says they mean, and the script proves it on its own output: W is the per-revolution magnification of every dimension, D the inner/outer-margin ratio of the generating curve, T the axial over radial movement of its centre, and the generating curve lies in the plane through the axis, so the shells are self-similar tubes rather than flat ribbons. The three defects of the first version are each named in the docstring and each is excluded by the self-test. Not higher because the primary paper was not consulted: the definitions are taken from two secondary restatements (which agree with each other on W, D and T up to Noshita's 2/(1+D) scaling of T, which is noted), the direction of the S ratio is the repository's convention rather than Raup's, and Raup's generating curve is an arbitrary aperture outline, here always an ellipse. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L20–L36: the four parameters defined, with the equations <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L20-L36>; create_raup_animations.py L96–L104: raup_shell(): a, r_c, z_c, generating curve in the radial-axial plane <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L96-L104>; create_raup_animations.py L38–L45: the three defects of the first version and how each is now excluded <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L38-L45>; create_raup_animations.py L134–L157: self_test(): recovery to 1e-9, spire monotone in T, planispiral one aperture thick <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L134-L157>; 1966-raup.py L28–L37: the same generating function in the minimal script <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/1966-raup.py#L28-L37>; datasets/raup/variables.json L134–L140: mathematical_formulation: the equations as implemented, with their source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/datasets/raup/variables.json#L134-L140>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Morphometric validation: 45/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Shape quantities are now measured on the rendered geometry - W, D and T recovered from each mesh, height/width and spire/width per panel - written to a CSV, printed, shown on the still, and re-derived independently in the measurements sidecar; recovered values equal the inputs to 5e-15 in the script's own check and, in the sidecar's independent derivation, exactly for W and T and to 3e-4 for D (the aperture's inner margin is read off a 100-point grid). That is validation of the implementation against the definitions, and it is complete. What the dimension also asks for - a comparison with specimens or with the paper's own figures - is absent: no published W, D, T of a real shell, and none of Raup's block-diagram placements, is compared with anything here. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L110–L131: recover_parameters(): W, D, T, height/width, spire/width from the mesh <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L110-L131>; create_raup_animations.py L189–L204: write_metrics(): the CSV <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L189-L204>; raup_shell_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): six rows, nominal and recovered values — raup_shell_metrics.csv: rendered output of create_raup_animations.py at ba6fd20, text/csv, 483 B, artifact_sha256 384d298d81f5373f754f790c2fa6560b93f8cf9164028a160b4df80810680057 (sha256 384d298d81f5373f754f790c2fa6560b93f8cf9164028a160b4df80810680057), spec_fingerprint 99d02b160418b61e3ca5605bf1327defebc58c14533242de5ba9809a805bf905. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): recovered translation rate T, 'Planispiral' (W=3.0, D=0.0, T=0.0) = 0.0 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.629, spire/width = 0.000; recovered distance from axis D, 'Planispiral' (W=3.0, D=0.0, T=0.0) = 0.0003 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Planispiral' (W=3.0, D=0.0, T=0.0) = 3.0 ratio (reference 3.0, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Turreted' (W=1.3, D=0.05, T=3.5) = 3.5 ratio (reference 3.5, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 1.142, spire/width = 0.858; recovered distance from axis D, 'Turreted' (W=1.3, D=0.05, T=3.5) = 0.0502 ratio (reference 0.05, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Turreted' (W=1.3, D=0.05, T=3.5) = 1.3 ratio (reference 1.3, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Evolute disc' (W=2.0, D=0.45, T=0.0) = 0.0 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.321, spire/width = 0.000; recovered distance from axis D, 'Evolute disc' (W=2.0, D=0.45, T=0.0) = 0.4501 ratio (reference 0.45, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Evolute disc' (W=2.0, D=0.45, T=0.0) = 2.0 ratio (reference 2.0, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Conical' (W=3.5, D=0.0, T=1.5) = 1.5 ratio (reference 1.5, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.805, spire/width = 0.481; recovered distance from axis D, 'Conical' (W=3.5, D=0.0, T=1.5) = 0.0003 ratio (reference 0.0, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Conical' (W=3.5, D=0.0, T=1.5) = 3.5 ratio (reference 3.5, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'High-spired' (W=1.6, D=0.1, T=2.5) = 2.5 ratio (reference 2.5, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.998, spire/width = 0.738; recovered distance from axis D, 'High-spired' (W=1.6, D=0.1, T=2.5) = 0.1002 ratio (reference 0.1, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'High-spired' (W=1.6, D=0.1, T=2.5) = 1.6 ratio (reference 1.6, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]; recovered translation rate T, 'Globose' (W=3.0, D=0.1, T=1.0) = 1.0 ratio (reference 1.0, Raup's definition of T (dz_c/dr_c), Noshita 2014 / Okabe & Yoshimura 2017; should equal the input) [Δz_c / Δr_c of the generating-curve centre over the last revolution of raup_shell()] — height/width = 0.628, spire/width = 0.341; recovered distance from axis D, 'Globose' (W=3.0, D=0.1, T=1.0) = 0.1002 ratio (reference 0.1, Raup's definition of D; should equal the input) [inner margin / outer margin of the aperture (min/max radial distance of the last generating curve)]; recovered whorl expansion W, 'Globose' (W=3.0, D=0.1, T=1.0) = 3.0 ratio (reference 3.0, Raup's definition of W; should equal the input) [centre distance from the axis at the aperture / one revolution earlier]." ;
