<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — MorphoEval overall 64.1/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "raup_shell(W, D, T, S) sweeps an ellipse of radial semi-axis a = a0 W^(theta/2pi) and axial semi-axis a/S, centred at r_c = a(1+D)/(1-D) from the axis and z_c = T r_c along it, in the plane through the axis. self_test() recovers W, D, T from meshes on a 3x3x4 grid to 4.9e-15 and checks the spire's axial travel rises strictly with T (the outer height/width may stay flat while the last whorl still envelops the spire, which is correct behaviour for involute forms); a T=0 shell is checked to be exactly one aperture thick. Six illustrative panels (W, D, T from variables.json) rendered rotating in side and overhead view; W x D and W x T sheets; a six-panel still with height/width; a CSV of nominal and recovered W, D, T per panel with height/width and spire/width. The measurements sidecar recovers W, D, T again, independently, from the script's generating function. Overall 64.1/100 (faithfulness 58.6, reproducibility 77.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit ba6fd20; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 80, Morphological realism / specimen match 45, Parameter expressivity 70, Morphometric validation 45, Source and data traceability 75, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 80. Output judged: raup_shell_animation.gif: rendered output of create_raup_animations.py at ba6fd20, image/gif, 15189434 B, 1200×800 px, 100 frames, artifact_sha256 986555a0032be189233cbf0ec15193959bf7f9cc0b1e099a6b7a289f7cff8b02 (sha256 986555a0032be189233cbf0ec15193959bf7f9cc0b1e099a6b7a289f7cff8b02), spec_fingerprint 99d02b160418b61e3ca5605bf1327defebc58c14533242de5ba9809a805bf905. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 99d02b160418b61e3ca5605bf1327defebc58c14533242de5ba9809a805bf905; artifact_sha256: 986555a0032be189233cbf0ec15193959bf7f9cc0b1e099a6b7a289f7cff8b02; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/raup/variables.json=c9c9cfaf70faa9a5...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-13-morphology-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Raup (1966), Noshita (2014), and Okabe & Yoshimura (2017) define logarithmic helicospiral shell coiling via whorl expansion W, radial distance D = r_min/r_max, translation T = dz_c/dr_c, and aperture shape S; reconstructed_in_script: Parametric 3D surface generator raup_shell(W, D, T, S) with exact inverse parameter recovery recover_parameters() to < 1e-14 error across a 3x3x4 morphospace grid; transfer_boundary: Six illustrative parameter sets in datasets/raup/variables.json labelled cf. canonical shell forms (planispiral, turreted, evolute disc, obconical, high-spired, globose); does_not_claim: Direct morphometric measurement of physical museum shell specimens or micro-CT meshes." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Obtain Raup 1966 and pin the definitions of W, D, T, S to its equations and figures; confirm the direction of the S ratio.",
        "remediation needed: Put a real shell beside at least one panel - a photograph, or a specimen's measured (W, D, T) from Raup 1967's ammonoid table or a later gastropod dataset - and measure the agreement.",
        "remediation needed: Report the stored frame count after saving the GIF, or write it with a writer that does not merge frames.",
        "remediation needed: Sweep S and D on their own in the parameter sheet; mark Raup's block-diagram regions (gastropods, ammonoids, bivalves, brachiopods) on the W x T and W x D sheets once the paper is in hand." ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.41e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Parameter expressivity: 70/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Each of W, D, T now has its own visible monotone effect, shown on two sheets (W x D at fixed T, W x T at fixed D) and on the 3 x 3 W x T slice of 1966-raup.py, and the self-test asserts the T effect. S is exposed in the function but not swept in any figure, and D is swept only together with W rather than on its own; the ranges on the sheets are the dataset's indicative bounds, not Raup's. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L236–L259: create_parameter_space_visualization(): the two sheets <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L236-L259>; 1966-raup.py L40–L71: W x T slice at fixed D <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/1966-raup.py#L40-L71>; create_raup_animations.py L147–L151: spire_over_width strictly increasing in T asserted <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L147-L151>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Reproducibility package: 80/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Deterministic (no RNG), no external data, a CLI with --frames, --fps, --no-gif, --self-test-only and --out-dir, a self-test that runs before any drawing and fails loudly, outputs that fill their panels, and the minimal script runs headless with --no-show/--out. numpy, matplotlib and Pillow are in requirements.txt and pinned in requirements.lock.txt. Not higher because the GIF is 16 MB and 100 frames for a 7 s loop, and because Pillow silently merges 20 of the 120 rendered frames, which the script does not report. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L280–L300: main(): CLI, self-test first <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L280-L300>; create_raup_animations.py L178–L183: fit_axes(): panels filled <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L178-L183>; 1966-raup.py L40–L44: --no-show / --out <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/1966-raup.py#L40-L44>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Source and data traceability: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Raup 1962, 1965 and 1966 are cited with DOIs (the 1966 JSTOR id, wrong in the dataset since 2025, is corrected), the two secondary sources the definitions actually come from are cited with DOIs and the specific statement used from each is given, and the dataset says plainly which of its earlier contents could not be verified and why they were replaced. Not higher because the primary paper was not read, so nothing here is pinned to a page or equation of Raup 1966, and because the parameter sets and ranges are the author's illustrative choices with no external source. Evidence: create_raup_animations.py L6–L18: citation block with DOIs; which definitions come from which secondary source <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L6-L18>; datasets/raup/README.md L1–L30: revision notice: what was unverifiable and what replaced it <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/datasets/raup/README.md#L1-L30>; datasets/raup/variables.json L10–L10: revision_2026_10_17 provenance note <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/datasets/raup/variables.json#L10-L10>; datasets/raup/paper_citations.bib L1–L70: DOIs added; JSTOR 1301992 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/datasets/raup/paper_citations.bib#L1-L70>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-raup-audit-raup-shell-coiling-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Raup shell coiling morphospace — Morphological realism / specimen match: 45/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The six forms are now distinct and each is what its name says (spire/width 0.00 for the two planispirals, 0.86 for the turreted form, 0.74 high-spired, 0.48 conical, 0.34 globose), and the panel titles and a figure footnote say that the taxon names are resemblances, not specimens. But there is still no real shell in the figure and no measured specimen the panels are tested against, which is what the dimension asks for; the labels are honest, not validated. Scored above the 30 of the first audit because the forms are no longer wrong, below the midpoint because nothing checks that a Turritella looks like the turreted panel. Evidence: raup_empirical_comparison.png (generated output, not in repo): six panels, each a different form; footnote on provenance — raup_empirical_comparison.png: rendered output of create_raup_animations.py at ba6fd20, image/png, 562658 B, 1630×1070 px, artifact_sha256 c50dbee57d0a64950d5470aed25583817eb8d39b97bcf2a7b89b991973f63ef7 (sha256 c50dbee57d0a64950d5470aed25583817eb8d39b97bcf2a7b89b991973f63ef7), spec_fingerprint 99d02b160418b61e3ca5605bf1327defebc58c14533242de5ba9809a805bf905; raup_shell_animation.gif (generated output, not in repo): side view: a tower, a cone, a disc, an involute coil; overhead: the log spirals — raup_shell_animation.gif: rendered output of create_raup_animations.py at ba6fd20, image/gif, 15189434 B, 1200×800 px, 100 frames, artifact_sha256 986555a0032be189233cbf0ec15193959bf7f9cc0b1e099a6b7a289f7cff8b02 (sha256 986555a0032be189233cbf0ec15193959bf7f9cc0b1e099a6b7a289f7cff8b02), spec_fingerprint 99d02b160418b61e3ca5605bf1327defebc58c14533242de5ba9809a805bf905; create_raup_animations.py L174–L176: ILLUSTRATIVE: the footnote text <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L174-L176>; datasets/raup/variables.json L66–L133: the six parameter sets with a note on why each value <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/datasets/raup/variables.json#L66-L133>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-raup-shell-coiling-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Code-to-model traceability: 80/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Each step is tied to its source as before, and the new section carries the same discipline: the docstring's item 7 says what is segmented, how, and what the anchors are; every segmentation constant (white threshold, background frame, core quantile, texture quantile, box, shadow cut) is a named parameter with a comment saying what it is for; the registration anchors are stated in terms of the dataset's landmark numbers; the figure's row F title names the figure each grid corresponds to. The trace still ends at Thompson's prose and drawing, the oblique/isogonal reading of Fig. 376 is still made by eye, and the declared box for the field photograph is a judgement recorded rather than derived. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L66–L83: item 7: what the outline test does and why <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L66-L83>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L590–L625: segment_field(): each parameter named and explained <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L590-L625>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L637–L643: anchors(): the rule for the peduncle in words <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L637-L643>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L181–L198: gpa(): orientation convention tied to Thompson's figures <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L181-L198>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L772–L775: row F titles name the figure each grid corresponds to <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L772-L775>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Model fidelity to source: 78/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-2> ;
    rdfs:comment "As before: \"coaxial circles\" formalised as the Moebius group with the reading stated, the oblique family added for Fig. 376 as drawn, the alternatives Thompson compares against (rectilinear coordinates) and does not (affine) fitted the same way, the thin-plate spline of Bookstein 1989 as the exact deformation, fitters checked on synthetic maps. Raised because the thing Thompson actually deformed - an outline - is now carried by each family and compared with a real outline, so curvature between the landmarks is no longer untested, and because the test is set up so that his family can only win by beating the no-deformation baseline, which is the comparison his sentence makes (\"rectilinear co-ordinates\" -> \"coaxial circles\" -> \"a very good outline\"). Not higher because his drawn grid is still displayed, not digitised and compared constant by constant; because the landmark test rests on genus means and the outline test on one individual per species, so neither is his \"typical Scaroid fish\"; and because the maps are fitted to the landmarks and only applied to the outline, so a map fitted to the outline itself (semilandmarks) is not tried. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L5–L23: the claim quoted; the reading of coaxial circles as a Moebius map <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L5-L23>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L47–L83: what is computed: the five families, noise floor, context, LOO, and item 7, the real outlines <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L47-L83>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L228–L289: moebius()/fit_moebius()/coaxial()/fit_coaxial(): the two coaxial families <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L228-L289>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L290–L310: tps_fit()/tps_apply(): Bookstein 1989 with bending energy <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L290-L310>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L323–L333: self_test(): known maps recovered <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L323-L333>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L701–L738: outline_analysis(): maps fitted to the species' landmarks, applied to the Scarus silhouette, scored against the Pomacanthus silhouette <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L701-L738>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-17-thompson-audit-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson's Scarus -> Pomacanthus coordinate transformation fitted to real species — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "To the landmark validation of the first audit (Procrustes distance, residual and explained share per family, within-genus noise floor, leave-one-landmark-out, depth/length and singular-value ratio, per-landmark residuals, all 3782 genus pairs, Scarus -> Chaetodon) the outline test adds two measurements on real silhouettes - IoU of the filled outlines and mean symmetric boundary distance - for every family against an explicit no-deformation baseline, so the question \"does the map help on the outline\" has a number and the answer is no for all five. The sidecar re-derives the IoU with a different rasteriser (agreement to 0.0001) and records the silhouette areas and the peduncle-anchor positions (0.79 and 0.84 of length). Not higher because there is still no published value to compare against (nobody has fitted this pair), one individual per species gives the outline numbers no spread, and digitising error on the landmarks is still not estimated. Evidence: thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L685–L700: silhouette_metrics(): IoU on a 1000-px raster and symmetric nearest-point boundary distance <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L685-L700>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L311–L322: all_fits(): residuals and explained shares (landmark test) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L311-L322>; thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py L898–L921: main(): per-family IoU, boundary distance, landmark RMS and the verdict against the baseline; thompson_outline_metrics.csv <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py#L898-L921>; morphoeval/measure_outputs.py L471–L567: measure_thompson_fish()/measure_thompson_outlines(): the landmark quantities and the independent IoU in the sidecar <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/morphoeval/measure_outputs.py#L471-L567>; thompson_outline_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): the five rows the figure and README quote — thompson_outline_metrics.csv: rendered output of thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py at 232e8f8, text/csv, 268 B, sha256 5faf2c6943c4de3b2dce92509b8cabc665dad0a1cec7c50cb7dcfecd84fd14c4; thompson_scarus_pomacanthus_outlines.png (generated output, not in repo): panel G — thompson_scarus_pomacanthus_outlines.png: rendered output of thompson/1917-thompson-scarus-pomacanthus.py at 232e8f8, image/png, 903004 B, 2520×1470 px, sha256 df6479f9f47f28fc341f29ff25d2dbf5a612e34215492d2c23cae956105a16f8. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): species in the landmark table = 791 count (reference 791, Friedman et al. 2019, Dryad 10.5061/dryad.fn457gr (Claverie & Wainwright 2014 landmarks), CC0: 'nearly 800 species') [rows of trimmed_tps_Claverie2014.csv (sha256 checked)]; Scarus species = 22 count [rows whose genus is Scarus]; Pomacanthus species = 9 count [rows whose genus is Pomacanthus]; Procrustes distance, Scarus mean to Pomacanthus mean = 0.0312 Procrustes units (RMS per landmark) [RMS landmark distance after optimal similarity superimposition of the genus means (unit centroid size)]; affine residual = 0.0259 Procrustes units [RMS after a least-squares affine map (6 parameters)] — explains 30.9 % of the Procrustes distance; Moebius residual (isogonal coaxial circles) = 0.0311 Procrustes units [RMS after a least-squares Moebius map z -> (az+b)/(cz+1), the conformal map that turns the Cartesian grid into two orthogonal pencils of coaxial circles] — explains 0.8 %: a conformal map cannot change the depth/length ratio; oblique coaxial-circle residual = 0.0256 Procrustes units [RMS after an affine map followed by z -> z/(cz+1) (8 parameters): coaxial circles whose two pencils need not be orthogonal, the family Thompson's Fig. 376 belongs to as drawn] — explains 32.4 %; thin-plate spline bending energy = 0.6778 dimensionless [bending energy of the exact TPS from the Scarus mean to the Pomacanthus mean (Bookstein 1989)]; within-Pomacanthus RMS (noise floor) = 0.0132 Procrustes units [RMS of the Pomacanthus species about their own Procrustes mean] — species range 0.0090-0.0180; within-Scarus 0.0099; leave-one-landmark-out RMS of the oblique coaxial family = 0.0371 Procrustes units [each landmark predicted by the 8-parameter map fitted to the other 16] — compare with the Procrustes distance: the family has no predictive value for held-out landmarks if it is not smaller; depth/length, Scarus mean = 0.3772 ratio [landmark extent in y over extent in x]; depth/length, Pomacanthus mean = 0.5873 ratio [landmark extent in y over extent in x]; percentile of Scarus -> Pomacanthus among all genus pairs (oblique coaxial, explained share) = 31.1475 percent [share of the 3782 ordered pairs of genus means (genera with >= 3 spp.) explained less well] — median pair 43 %; Scarus -> Chaetodon spp., median explained by oblique coaxial circles = 35.12 percent [median over the 54 Chaetodon species] — range 12-61 %; silhouette area, Scarus ghobban = 214862 pixels [segmented mask at 0.25 scale; photograph SHA-256 732f1e68da7e... checked by the script]; caudal-peduncle anchor, Scarus ghobban = 0.7919 fraction of silhouette length [x of the peduncle anchor between the anterior-most and posterior-most mask columns (fish facing left)] — plausible range for a perciform fish ~0.75-0.90; the anchor fixes the registration of the landmarks to the photograph; silhouette area, Pomacanthus semicirculatus = 92699 pixels [segmented mask at 0.25 scale; photograph SHA-256 5622e415149a... checked by the script]; caudal-peduncle anchor, Pomacanthus semicirculatus = 0.8395 fraction of silhouette length [x of the peduncle anchor between the anterior-most and posterior-most mask columns (fish facing left)] — plausible range for a perciform fish ~0.75-0.90; the anchor fixes the registration of the landmarks to the photograph; silhouette IoU, similarity = 0.662 ratio (reference 0.6619, the script's own IoU (skimage.draw.polygon, 1000-px grid)) [Scarus ghobban silhouette carried by the map fitted to the 17 landmarks of S. ghobban -> P. semicirculatus, against the P. semicirculatus silhouette; point-in-polygon on a 900 x 900 grid (independent of the script's rasteriser)] — boundary distance 0.0404 = 5.6 % of body length; landmark RMS 0.0388; the no-deformation baseline; silhouette IoU, affine = 0.6515 ratio (reference 0.6515, the script's own IoU (skimage.draw.polygon, 1000-px grid)) [Scarus ghobban silhouette carried by the map fitted to the 17 landmarks of S. ghobban -> P. semicirculatus, against the P. semicirculatus silhouette; point-in-polygon on a 900 x 900 grid (independent of the script's rasteriser)] — boundary distance 0.0466 = 6.5 % of body length; landmark RMS 0.0322; silhouette IoU, moebius = 0.6449 ratio (reference 0.6448, the script's own IoU (skimage.draw.polygon, 1000-px grid)) [Scarus ghobban silhouette carried by the map fitted to the 17 landmarks of S. ghobban -> P. semicirculatus, against the P. semicirculatus silhouette; point-in-polygon on a 900 x 900 grid (independent of the script's rasteriser)] — boundary distance 0.0427 = 5.9 % of body length; landmark RMS 0.0381; silhouette IoU, coaxial = 0.6185 ratio (reference 0.6184, the script's own IoU (skimage.draw.polygon, 1000-px grid)) [Scarus ghobban silhouette carried by the map fitted to the 17 landmarks of S. ghobban -> P. semicirculatus, against the P. semicirculatus silhouette; point-in-polygon on a 900 x 900 grid (independent of the script's rasteriser)] — boundary distance 0.0509 = 7.0 % of body length; landmark RMS 0.0303; silhouette IoU, tps = 0.6287 ratio (reference 0.6287, the script's own IoU (skimage.draw.polygon, 1000-px grid)) [Scarus ghobban silhouette carried by the map fitted to the 17 landmarks of S. ghobban -> P. semicirculatus, against the P. semicirculatus silhouette; point-in-polygon on a 900 x 900 grid (independent of the script's rasteriser)] — boundary distance 0.0477 = 6.6 % of body length; landmark RMS 0.0000." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
