<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-v2-vogel-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) & Douady–Couder (1992) Golden-Angle Phyllotaxis — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/vogel-phyllotaxis-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/vogel-phyllotaxis-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/vogel-phyllotaxis-3> ;
    rdfs:comment "Vogel's (1979) planar spiral law, rising Fibonacci parastichy cascade (8,13)->(13,21)->(21,34)->(34,55), Lucas (29,47)->(47,76) branch, and bijugate 2*(21,34) = (42,68) whorls are reproduced and verified by Delaunay contact-graph topology. Douady & Couder's (1992) Hofmeister repulsive energy minimization converges from disparate initial angles (175 deg and 130 deg -> 137.59 deg; 99.8 deg -> 99.38 deg), and the noisy rim-dislocation ensemble mechanistically links outer-rim contact chain loss to Swinton et al.'s (2016) Fib-1 > Fib+1 grain-defect bias. Evidence: 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L110–L154: vogel_spiral(): exact planar spiral and multijugate whorl generator <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L110-L154>; 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L383–L441: simulate_douady_couder_hofmeister(): Hofmeister repulsive energy minimization <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L383-L441>; 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L470–L562: simulate_swinton_dislocation_ensemble(): rim contact-chain loss mechanism <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L470-L562>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-vogel-phyllotaxis-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-v2-vogel-phyllotaxis-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) & Douady–Couder (1992) Golden-Angle Phyllotaxis — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Bounded Voronoi polygon clipping with 72 outer guard vertices completely resolves the v1 unbounded-cell artifact: `rational_120.0` now scores `voronoi_cv_area = 0.6207` and `mean_circularity = 0.0284`, while the golden angle (`137.5078 deg`) simultaneously minimizes `voronoi_cv_area` (`0.007209`), minimizes `nnd_cv` (`0.011108`), and maximizes Voronoi circularity (`0.852513`). All 7 morphometrics are independently verified in `2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-v2.measurements.yaml`. Evidence: 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L223–L303: compute_packing_metrics(): bounded Voronoi cells with guard ring & disk clipping <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L223-L303>; 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py L634–L654: run_self_tests(): asserts golden angle beats 137.3, 137.6, and 120.0 deg on all 3 metrics <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L634-L654>; vogel_phyllotaxis_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): 6 regimes including empirical_specimen_helianthus_jpg — vogel_phyllotaxis_metrics.csv: rendered output of 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py at c89d18d, text/csv, 449 B, artifact_sha256 cb2404142073f9a5eb7b9b03af60891ce8efd46cca9956dc64caed92a6fe3f71 (sha256 cb2404142073f9a5eb7b9b03af60891ce8efd46cca9956dc64caed92a6fe3f71), spec_fingerprint 5df8c2b4cc4b9b4a86ea26aace00ebd26df8456a62d99c23287ddcea2644e06c. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): golden divergence angle α₀ = 360°/τ² = 137.5078 degrees (reference 137.50776405003785, Vogel 1979 Mathematical Biosciences 44:179 Eq. (1)-(4)) [exact golden-section divergence angle 360 * (2 - τ)]; outer-annulus [14.5, 22.5) opposed contact parastichy ratio (n/m) = 1.6177 ratio (55/34) (reference 1.61765, Vogel 1979 / Swinton et al. 2016 R. Soc. Open Sci. 3:160091 §2.3) [Delaunay contact parastichy pair (34, 55) in outer annulus r in [14.5, 22.5)] — full radial cascade: [(8, 13), (13, 21), (21, 34), (34, 55)]; Voronoi cell area CV at golden angle (137.5078°) = 0.0072 CV (std/mean) (reference 0.009777076602327238, Vogel 1979 Fig. 2a negative control (α = 137.30°)) [Voronoi polygon area dispersion across interior florets (0.18 R_max <= r <= 0.85 R_max, N=450)] — strictly lower than α=137.30° (0.0098) and α=137.60° (0.0074); Douady & Couder (1992) Hofmeister main-branch emergent divergence angle = 137.586 degrees (reference 137.507764, Douady & Couder 1992 Phys. Rev. Lett. 68:2098 Fig. 3) [mean steady-state divergence angle over final 25 plastochrons on main Fibonacci branch (G: 0.55 -> 0.04)]; Douady & Couder (1992) Hofmeister Lucas-branch emergent divergence angle = 99.38 degrees (reference 99.501553, Douady & Couder 1992 Phys. Rev. Lett. 68:2098 / 1996 J. Theor. Biol. 178:255) [mean steady-state divergence angle over final 25 plastochrons on secondary Lucas branch (G: 0.22 -> 0.04)]; Swinton et al. (2016) photoreviewed Fibonacci-structure prevalence = 82.29 percent (reference 82.29, Swinton, Ochu & MSI Turing's Sunflower Consortium 2016 R. Soc. Open Sci. 3:160091 Table 1) [632 of 768 photoreviewed Helianthus annuus parastichy counts belonging to Fibonacci, Lucas, Double-Fib, or F4 sequences] — Fib-1 (49) vs Fib+1 (17) one-sided binomial p = 5.07e-05; empirical specimen photograph segmented floret Voronoi circularity ⟨4πA/P²⟩ = 0.7934 ratio (4πA/P²) (reference 0.8525133755444986, helianthus_annuus_capitulum_specimen.jpg (File:Sunflower Spiral.jpg, CC BY-SA 2.0)) [Difference-of-Gaussians floret segmentation (N=621 florets, 402 interior Voronoi cells) on helianthus_annuus_capitulum_specimen.jpg] — specimen Voronoi area CV = 0.2530, hex neighbor fraction = 0.377; mechanistic rim-dislocation ensemble Pearson r vs Swinton (2016) Table 1 = 0.995 Pearson r (reference 1.0, Swinton, Ochu & MSI Turing's Sunflower Consortium 2016 R. Soc. Open Sci. 3:160091 Table 1) [correlation across 6 parastichy classes (N=768 simulated vs N=768 photoreviewed; Fib-1=68 > Fib+1=22, p=6.25e-07)]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-vogel-phyllotaxis-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-v2-vogel-phyllotaxis-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-v2-vogel-phyllotaxis-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-v2-vogel-phyllotaxis-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-v2-vogel-phyllotaxis-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-v2-vogel-phyllotaxis-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-v2-vogel-phyllotaxis-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-v2-vogel-phyllotaxis-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-v2-vogel-phyllotaxis-8> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit-v2-vogel-phyllotaxis-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) & Douady–Couder (1992) Golden-Angle Phyllotaxis — MorphoEval overall 85.9/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Remediated v2 reproduction of Vogel (1979) and Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) golden-angle phyllotaxis validated against Swinton et al. (2016) Royal Society Helianthus annuus parastichy data and direct Difference-of-Gaussians floret segmentation on a real capitulum photograph (621 segmented florets, 402 interior Voronoi cells, mean circularity 0.793 vs 0.853 model). All four defects surfaced in the v1 dual-agent audit are resolved and verified by automated assertions in `run_self_tests()`. Overall 85.9/100 (faithfulness 84.7, reproducibility 88.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit c89d18d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: vogel_phyllotaxis_comparison.png: rendered output of 1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py at c89d18d, image/png, 2217939 B, 2960×1840 px, artifact_sha256 3ab57a6be31aab64ec4cfa6db34f77b8f19cb2744a812f3fba01a6c8f26f1c3c (sha256 3ab57a6be31aab64ec4cfa6db34f77b8f19cb2744a812f3fba01a6c8f26f1c3c), spec_fingerprint 5df8c2b4cc4b9b4a86ea26aace00ebd26df8456a62d99c23287ddcea2644e06c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 5df8c2b4cc4b9b4a86ea26aace00ebd26df8456a62d99c23287ddcea2644e06c; artifact_sha256: 3ab57a6be31aab64ec4cfa6db34f77b8f19cb2744a812f3fba01a6c8f26f1c3c; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/phyllotaxis/helianthus_annuus_capitulum_specimen.jpg=c76483eea3e564fe..., datasets/phyllotaxis/helianthus_parastichy_annotated.jpg=7cd34354e23584cb..., datasets/phyllotaxis/phyllotaxis_reference.json=432d1eeebf62bdc7...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-18-phyllotaxis-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Vogel (1979) defines planar capitulum spiral placement r_n = c*sqrt(n), theta_n = n*alpha_0 with golden divergence angle alpha_0 = 360/tau^2 = 137.507764 deg | Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) demonstrate self-organized convergence of repulsive Hofmeister primordia on a radially advecting meristem ring to the golden and Lucas noble angles | Swinton, Ochu & MSI Turing's Sunflower Consortium (2016) report 768 photoreviewed parastichy counts across 657 Helianthus annuus heads (82.3% Fibonacci structure; 49 Fib-1 vs 17 Fib+1, binomial p = 5.07e-5); reconstructed_in_script: Planar Vogel spiral generator, Delaunay/Voronoi rising Fibonacci parastichy cascade (8,13)->(13,21)->(21,34)->(34,55), bounded Voronoi area CV & circularity optimality, Douady-Couder Hofmeister relaxation, DoG floret segmentation on helianthus_annuus_capitulum_specimen.jpg, and rim-dislocation ensemble reproducing Fib-1 > Fib+1; transfer_boundary: Outer-rim Delaunay contact-chain loss on noisy capitula used to model the empirical excess of Fibonacci-1 over Fibonacci+1 counts in Swinton et al. (2016); does_not_claim: Full 3D auxin PIN1 transport PDE simulation on a curved dome (uses Vogel's kinematic spiral and Douady & Couder's effective Hofmeister inhibitory potential)." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-vogel-phyllotaxis> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the Douady–Couder Hofmeister potential directly to a continuum auxin-PIN1 reaction-advection-diffusion solver on the meristematic dome (Jönsson et al. 2006 / Newell et al. 2008).",
        "remediation needed: Extend specimen image analysis from 2D planar projection to 3D dome surface profilometry when micro-CT capitulum scans become available." ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.59e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

