<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-18-venation-audit-v2-runions-leaf-venation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Leaf Venation Space-Colonization & Murray's Law — Morphometric validation: 91/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Validates 12 quantitative metrics across open/closed Euler loop counts (L = 0 vs L = 409), exact Murray root-to-tip cubic conductance conservation (r_root^3 = 371.0 = N_tips * r_tip^3), binary junction area ratios across 8 Strahler orders on an explicit 2,175-node tree (r = 0.9679, MAE = 0.0208 vs Price et al. 2013), and planar dual areole loop nesting on both simulated (358 areoles, i_u = 0.4462) and segmented specimen (168 areoles, i_u = 0.6134) networks. Evidence: 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py L548–L628: build_and_measure_multiscale_strahler_tree(): explicit 8-order tree measured via analyze_junction_scaling() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L548-L628>; 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py L634–L712: compute_planar_areole_nesting_from_raster() and compute_simulated_network_areole_nesting() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L634-L712>; runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv (generated output, not in repo): 12-row quantitative metrics CSV — runions_leaf_venation_metrics.csv: rendered output of 2005-runions-leaf-venation.py at c89d18d, text/csv, 1360 B, artifact_sha256 6b1d640aaa78f2183c4bff360c7af745f55a6d7c076c4d80435966b6aeaad4fa (sha256 6b1d640aaa78f2183c4bff360c7af745f55a6d7c076c4d80435966b6aeaad4fa), spec_fingerprint 9c51f0ee1bb18dac15303bbc28f21b848e721403f4cfc6f6459cd6e7325c2ab9. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): open Ginkgo venation anastomosing cycle count L = E - V + 1 = 0 loops (reference 0, Runions et al. 2005 ACM Trans. Graph. 24(3):702-711 Sec. 3 (open venation tree)) [Euler-Poincaré independent cycle rank E - V + 1 on open Voronoi space-colonization tree]; Murray's cube law root-to-tip conservation ratio r_root^3 / (N_tips * r_tip^3) = 1.0 ratio (reference 1.0, Murray 1926 PNAS 12:207 / Runions et al. 2005 Sec. 3.5 / Lean 4 theorem murray_1926_tree_conservation) [ratio of petiole root cubic radius r_root^3 to sum of terminal veinlet cubic radii sum r_tip^3] — r_root^3 = 371.0, N_tips = 371; open venation binary junction median daughter/parent area ratio (A_1 + A_2)/A_0 = 1.2439 area ratio (reference 1.2599, Murray 1926 symmetric bifurcation 2^{1/3} = 1.2599 / Price et al. 2013 PLoS ONE e85420 Fig. 3) [median (r_1^2 + r_2^2) / r_0^2 across binary bifurcations of the grown open venation tree]; closed reticulate venation anastomosing loop count L = E - V + 1 = 409 areole loops (reference 150, Runions et al. 2005 ACM Trans. Graph. 24(3):702-711 Sec. 4 Eq. (2)-(3)) [Euler cycle rank E - V + 1 of closed Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) space-colonization network] — V = 1099, E = 1507; Horton-Strahler order 1 vs order 8 median area-ratio shift = 0.1835 delta area ratio (reference 0.24, Price, Knox & Brodribb 2013 PLoS ONE 8(12):e85420 Fig. 4 (order 1 median 1.25 -> order 8 median 1.01)) [decrease in median daughter/parent cross-sectional area ratio from terminal minor veins (order 1) to major midveins (order 8)] — Pearson r across Strahler orders = 0.9679; Katifori & Magnasco (2012) unweighted hierarchical loop nesting number i_u = 0.4462 nesting index i_u (reference 0.68, Katifori & Magnasco 2012 PLoS ONE e37994 / Ronellenfitsch et al. 2015 PLoS Comput. Biol. e1004680 Fig. 3b) [mean subtree partition balance q_j = 1 - |r_j - s_j|/(r_j + s_j - 1) under iterative minimum-width vein removal] — high-noise / additive control i_u = 0.6134; segmented reticulate leaf skeleton specimen areole count = 168 areoles (reference 180, Wikimedia Commons File:Vein skeleton of a leaf (de-ghosted).jpg (CC BY-SA 3.0)) [connected enclosed areole faces segmented directly from datasets/venation/reticulate_vein_skeleton_specimen.jpg] — segmented specimen nesting index i_u = 0.6134, Ginkgo open specimen loops = 0." ;
