<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Code-to-model traceability: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Every geometric function states its exact volume $V$, active calcifying surface area $S$, and resulting one-step algebraic relation in its docstring, and the module docstring summarizes the four geometries' $(S:V, C, \\text{SAP})$ scaling regimes in a table mapped to Appendix A / Results and Figs. 3 & 6 of Kahng et al. (2024). Deduct 15 points because exact equation numbers from Kahng et al. (2024) Appendix A are not cited per function, and deduct 10 points because the distinction between discrete 1-yr difference equations and continuous ODE rates is not noted in `hemisphere_extension`. Evidence: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L25–L31: summary table mapping 4 coral geometries to S:V, C, and SAP trends <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L25-L31>; 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L68–L110: per-function V and S formulas referencing Appendix A / Results <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L68-L110>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Model fidelity to source: 74/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "All seven algebraic functions (`hemisphere_extension`, `hemisphere_sap`, `disc_extension`, `disc_sap`, `cone_extension`, `cone_sap`, `cylinder_sap`, L68-110) are exact consequences of the paper's discrete annual volume rule `V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho` under the stated surface/volume formulas (`V = 2/3 pi r^3, S = 2 pi r^2`; `V = h pi r^2, S = pi r^2`; `V = pi h^3/(3 alpha^2), S = pi h^2 sqrt(1+alpha^2)/alpha^2`; `V = pi r^2 L, S = 2 pi r L`). Deduct 14 points because the script does not contrast the finite 1-yr step (`r(t+1) - r(t)`, which rises from `0.52` to `1.20 cm/yr` in Panel c) against the instantaneous continuum limit `dr/dt = G/rho = 1.25 cm/yr` (where hemisphere linear extension is strictly size-independent); and deduct 12 points because general oblate/prolate hemispheroids and multi-branch colony self-shading are simplified to a spherical hemisphere and single cylinder without explicit boundary notes. Evidence: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L57–L60: empirical parameter dictionaries MASSIVE, BRANCH, DISC, and COMMON <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L57-L60>; 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L68–L110: exact discrete 1-year extension and SAP formulas for hemisphere, disc, cone, and cylinder <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L68-L110>; 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L172–L185: panel (c) plots discrete 1-yr extension approaching continuum plateau G/rho and sqrt(2)*G/rho <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L172-L185>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Morphometric validation: 38/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Computes and reports asymptotic linear extensions (`1.28 cm/yr` for massive *Porites*; `2.00, 2.53, 3.99, 7.36 cm/yr` for *Acropora* cones with `alpha = 0.5..4`), size-independent SAP (`0.114 /yr` for *Leptoseris* disc; `7.143 /yr` for *Acropora* cylinder), and the `18.9x` (`~19x`) microfragmentation SAP ratio between `r = 1 cm` (`1.86 /yr`) and `r = 25 cm` (`0.10 /yr`). Deduct 42 points because no empirical colony growth dataset (e.g., Lough 2008 *Porites* cores, Hughes 1987 *Acropora*, or Kahng 2023 *Leptoseris* measurements) is loaded to compute residuals or $R^2$; and deduct 20 points because no CSV table or automated `--self-test` verification is emitted. Evidence: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L215–L236: computes sap_small (r=1 cm), sap_large (r=25 cm), and ~19x microfragmentation ratio <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L215-L236>; 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L250–L264: console verification printout of asymptotic C and size-independent SAP <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L250-L264>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): massive Porites hemisphere linear extension C at r = 30 cm (discrete 1-yr step) = 1.2301 cm/yr (reference 1.2812, Kahng, Odle & Wakeman 2024 PeerJ 12:e17037 Appendix A (continuum C = G/rho = 1.2812 cm/yr)) [hemisphere_extension(r=30 cm, G=1.64, rho=1.28) = (r^3 + 3*G*r^2/rho)^(1/3) - r] — at r = 1 cm discrete step gives C = 0.6920 cm/yr due to 1-yr forward-Euler discretization; massive Porites microfragmentation SAP speedup ratio (r = 1 cm vs r = 25 cm) = 18.6207 SAP(1 cm) / SAP(25 cm) (reference 18.92, Kahng, Odle & Wakeman 2024 PeerJ 12:e17037 (SAP(1 cm)=1.8558/yr vs SAP(25 cm)=0.0981/yr)) [hemisphere_sap(r=1 cm) / hemisphere_sap(r=25 cm) for G=1.64, rho=1.28]; deep-water Leptoseris flat-disc size-independent SAP (h = 0.20 cm) = 0.1142 yr^-1 (reference 0.1142, Kahng, Odle & Wakeman 2024 PeerJ 12:e17037 / Kahng 2023) [disc_sap(G=0.061, rho=2.67, h=0.20) = G / (rho * h)]; branching Acropora cylinder size-independent SAP (r = 0.50 cm) = 7.1429 yr^-1 (reference 7.1429, Kahng, Odle & Wakeman 2024 PeerJ 12:e17037 / Hughes 1987) [cylinder_sap(G=2.50, rho=1.40, r=0.50) = 2 * G / (rho * r)]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-4> ;
    pk:hasProbability 3.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — MorphoEval overall 60.2/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "`2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py` faithfully encodes the discrete annual volume-accretion master rule `V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho` and the four idealized geometric families from Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) (hemispheroid, cone, flat disc, and cylinder), reproducing their surface-area productivity (`SAP = dS/S`), linear extension (`C`), aspect-ratio dependence (Fig. 3), diameter/thickness scaling, and the ~19x microfragmentation SAP speedup for massive *Porites* (`r = 1 cm` vs `r = 25 cm`). Its main limitations are that the finite 1-year step introduces small-radius curvature in hemisphere/cone extension (`C = 0.52 -> 1.25 cm/yr` vs the exact continuum `dr/dt = G/rho = 1.25 cm/yr`), the equal-`G, rho` comparison applies `G = 1.50 g cm^-2 yr^-1` to a thin `h = 0.5 cm` disc (producing `26 cm/yr` extension at `r = 30 cm`), and no empirical colony growth tables or coral specimen photographs are overlaid. Overall 60.2/100 (faithfulness 54.6, reproducibility 73.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5564750; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 74, Morphological realism / specimen match 42, Parameter expressivity 72, Morphometric validation 38, Source and data traceability 74, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 72. Output judged: kahng_coral_geometry_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py at 5564750, image/png, 282553 B, 1774×1267 px, artifact_sha256 fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812 (sha256 fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812), spec_fingerprint 833cc6f3d6f3988fa15a852dd8366b15c68ef56d6fd98635b3250ff241f4746a. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 833cc6f3d6f3988fa15a852dd8366b15c68ef56d6fd98635b3250ff241f4746a; artifact_sha256: fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024): colony volume increment V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho implies that surface-area productivity (SAP = dS/S) and linear extension C are governed by how S:V scales with colony size across hemispheroids, cones, flat discs, and cylinders; reconstructed_in_script: Exact 1-year discrete volume-step algebraic functions for hemisphere, fixed-aspect cone, fixed-thickness flat disc, and fixed-diameter cylinder (`hemisphere_extension`, `hemisphere_sap`, `disc_extension`, `disc_sap`, `cone_extension`, `cone_sap`, `cylinder_sap`), 6-panel comparative figure, and 15-year log-area animation; transfer_boundary: Uses a finite 1-year step V(t+1) = V(t) + G*S(t)/rho without comparing against the continuum differential limit (dV/dt = G*S/rho, where hemisphere dR/dt = G/rho is strictly constant at all radii), and uses schematic 2D matplotlib patches rather than 3D coral colony meshes or empirical growth time series; does_not_claim: 3D hydrodynamic polyp-scale morphogenesis or direct statistical fitting to raw field colony time series." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py:68-110,172-185 Plot the exact continuum differential extension rates (dr/dt = G/rho for hemisphere, dh/dt = G*sqrt(1+alpha^2)/rho for cone, dr/dt = G*r/(2*rho*h) for disc) alongside the discrete 1-year Euler step curves, and use realistic DISC parameters (or dual y-axes) in Panel (c).",
        "remediation needed: Vendor `datasets/kahng/` with SHA-256-pinned empirical growth tables from Lough (2008), Hughes (1987), and Kahng (2023) / Kahng et al. (2024), overlay observed colony extension/SAP data points, and add `--self-test` and CSV metrics export." ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.02e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Parameter expressivity: 72/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Sweeps colony size `0.5..30 cm` across all four geometries (Panels b, c), sweeps cone aspect ratio `alpha in {0.5, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0}` (Panel d), sweeps cylinder branch diameter `0.3..4.0 cm` and disc plate thickness `0.05..1.5 cm` (Panel e), and contrasts species-specific calcification regimes (`MASSIVE`, `BRANCH`, `DISC`) with the shape-isolating `COMMON` regime. Deduct 18 points because no model parameters (`G`, `rho`, `alpha`, `h`, `r`, `years`) are configurable via CLI flags (L320-331), and deduct 10 points because step size `dt` is fixed to `1 yr`. Evidence: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L158–L211: sweeps over colony size, cone aspect ratio alpha, branch diameter 2r, and plate thickness h <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L158-L211>; 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L320–L331: CLI exposes only -o/--output, --no-show, and --gif <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L320-L331>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Reproducibility package: 72/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Completely deterministic (no RNG), runs in < 1 s under the locked environment (`requirements.lock.txt`), and provides `-o/--output`, `--no-show`, and `--gif` CLI flags. Deduct 12 points for lacking a `--self-test` flag and CSV metrics output; deduct 8 points because `--gif` is omitted from the docstring usage examples (L38-41) and `show=True` is the default; and deduct 8 points because Pillow deduplicates the trailing hold frames (`frames += [frames[-1]] * (fps * 2)` at L314) from 24 to 16 frames on disk. Evidence: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L38–L41: docstring CLI usage block <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L38-L41>; 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L314–L331: GIF save and argparse CLI entrypoint <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L314-L331>; requirements.lock.txt L1–L51: locked dependencies in requirements.lock.txt <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L51>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Source and data traceability: 74/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Module docstring records full authors, title, journal (`PeerJ 12:e17037`), year, PMCID (`PMC10909345`), resolving DOI (`10.7717/peerj.17037`), and upstream GitHub repository (`github.com/ericodle/coral_geometry_modeling`), plus inline attribution to Raup & Graus (1972), Lough (2008), Hughes (1987), and Kahng (2023). Deduct 16 points because no `datasets/kahng/` directory, `README.md`, or `paper_citations.bib` with full DOIs for the empirical parameter sources (Lough 2008, Hughes 1987, Kahng 2023) is vendored; and deduct 10 points because the upstream `ericodle/coral_geometry_modeling` commit hash is not pinned. Evidence: 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L5–L10: complete citation, PMCID, DOI 10.7717/peerj.17037, and upstream GitHub repo URL <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L5-L10>; 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L57–L60: parameter attributions to Lough 2008, Hughes 1987, Kahng 2023, and paper Fig. 6 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L57-L60>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-kahng-coral-geometry-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Kahng, Odle & Wakeman (2024) Reef-Coral Colony Geometry & Surface-Area Productivity — Morphological realism / specimen match: 42/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Panel (a) draws clear 2D geometric glyphs annotated with `(V, S, S:V trend)` for the four coral growth forms, Panels (b-e) reproduce the analytical curves of Kahng et al. (2024) (including Fig. 3 cone aspect ratios and Fig. 6 shape comparisons), and the GIF animates 15 years of hemisphere and cone cross-sectional growth alongside log surface-area trajectories. Deduct 35 points because no real coral colony photographs, CT-scanned 3D colony meshes, or digitized empirical data points from *Porites*, *Acropora*, or *Leptoseris* are overlaid; and deduct 23 points because in Panel (c) and the GIF, applying `COMMON` (`G=1.50, rho=1.20`) to a `0.5 cm` flat disc drives disc extension to `26.1 cm/yr` at `r = 30 cm` and area to `~10^9 cm^2` at year 15, visually dwarfing the realistic hemisphere and cone curves. Evidence: kahng_coral_geometry_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): 6-panel analytical figure with 2D shape glyphs and SAP/extension curves — kahng_coral_geometry_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py at 5564750, image/png, 282553 B, 1774×1267 px, artifact_sha256 fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812 (sha256 fa8ce6cd95b493eee42054724462d8d7e6380dd161cc7899a464457cd765f812), spec_fingerprint 833cc6f3d6f3988fa15a852dd8366b15c68ef56d6fd98635b3250ff241f4746a; docs/media/kahng_coral_geometry_growth.gif (generated output, not in repo): 16-unique-frame animation of 15-year colony growth and log-area trajectories — docs/media/kahng_coral_geometry_growth.gif: rendered output of 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py at 5564750, image/gif, 248080 B, 720×300 px, 16 frames, artifact_sha256 6d2629a5bb1c8f33c60c72f9efa435dd70cdefc0e7c5cbb050c7a50bb1ac50d0 (sha256 6d2629a5bb1c8f33c60c72f9efa435dd70cdefc0e7c5cbb050c7a50bb1ac50d0), spec_fingerprint 833cc6f3d6f3988fa15a852dd8366b15c68ef56d6fd98635b3250ff241f4746a; 2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py L116–L147: _draw_glyphs schematic 2D patches <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2024-kahng-coral-geometry.py#L116-L147>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-kahng-coral-geometry-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — Code-to-model traceability: 50/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Functions are compact and clearly structured into Section (1) (`diffusion_length`, `hex_lattice`, citing Petroff Eq. 2 and Fig. 4) and Section (2) (`_resample`, `_advance_front`, `grow_stromatolite`, `aspect_ratio`). Deduct 25 points because the docstring and console printout display the small-slope KPZ PDE `dh/dt = v + lambda * (1 + 1/2 (dh/dr)^2)` (L34, L85, L296) while `_advance_front` actually integrates a Lagrangian normal+vertical velocity modulated by `w_photic` and Laplacian smoothing; and deduct 25 points because the constants `0.12` and `0.88` in `w_photic` (L130) and `smooth = 0.03` (L147) have no source equation provenance. Evidence: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L64–L74: docstrings cite Petroff Eq. 2 and Fig. 4 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L64-L74>; 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L85–L98: header explains transition from graph KPZ equation to Lagrangian front v*z_hat + lambda*n_hat <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L85-L98>; 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L126–L143: untraced w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z_max)^2 and 3-point smoothing <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L126-L143>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — Model fidelity to source: 44/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Correctly evaluates the diffusive spacing relation `ell = alpha * sqrt(D * tau)` (L64-67) and hexagonal lattice geometry (L70-81). However, (-22) the lamina cross-section model (L113-163) does not solve Petroff et al.'s (2010) diffusive nutrient field (`nabla^2 c = 0`) or flux-driven lamina growth (`v_n prop dc/dn`), so the top row (diffusion spacing) and bottom row (lamina shapes) are mathematically uncoupled; (-14) relative to the Batchelor et al. (2004) equation cited in the docstring (`dh/dt = v + lambda*(1 + 1/2 (dh/dr)^2)`, L34, L296), `_advance_front` introduces an uncited quadratic photic crest weight `w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88 * (z / z.max())**2` (L130), pins the basal endpoints at `+-base_half` (L136-137), and applies a 3-point Laplacian smoothing filter (L141-142); and (-8) the text panel states that `ell ~ 0.66 cm` records a `~20 h` rhythmic metabolism (L238-239) whereas `0.66 cm` was computed from `tau = 12 h` (L193, L235). Evidence: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L64–L81: diffusion_length ell = alpha*sqrt(D*tau) and hex_lattice <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L64-L81>; 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L113–L143: _advance_front uses ad-hoc w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z_max)^2, pinned base, and 3-point smoothing instead of Petroff diffusive flux or pure Batchelor KPZ <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L113-L143>; 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L233–L240: text panel computes ell = 0.66 cm from tau = 12 h but prose says '~20 h rhythmic metabolism' <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L233-L240>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — Morphometric validation: 25/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Computes `diffusion_length` at `tau in {3, 6, 12, 24} h` and `aspect_ratio` (`height / width`) on the top lamina of each grown profile (`0.6716`, `1.1674`, `2.6177` for `beta = 0.3, 1.5, 5.0`). Deduct 40 points because no empirical cone-spacing measurements (Yellowstone modern mats, lab cultures, or Archean/Proterozoic fossils from Petroff et al. Table 1 / Fig. 2-3) are loaded or compared statistically; deduct 20 points because flank angle, apex curvature radius, and axial lamina thickening ratio are not measured; and deduct 15 points because the `0.5-1.5 cm` shaded band in Panel (a) (L198) is hardcoded rather than derived from a dataset. Evidence: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L165–L171: aspect_ratio computes height/width for figure annotation only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L165-L171>; 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L198–L198: hardcoded axhspan(0.5, 1.5) in panel (a) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L198-L198>; 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L290–L298: console printout of diffusion_length for tau = 3, 6, 12, 24 h <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L290-L298>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): field cone spacing ell at tau = 12 h (D = 1e-5 cm^2/s, alpha = 1.0) = 0.6573 cm (reference 1.0, Petroff et al. 2010 PNAS 107(22):9956-9961 Eq. 2 (~1 cm Yellowstone field spacing)) [diffusion_length(12 * 3600, D=1e-5, alpha=1.0) = alpha * sqrt(D * tau)] — lab clumps (alpha=0.30) ell(12 h) = 0.1972 cm; hex_lattice min NN distance = 0.6573 cm; dome regime (beta = 0.3) final lamina height/width aspect ratio = 0.6692 height/width [aspect_ratio(grow_stromatolite(v=0.3, lam=1.0)[-1])]; cone regime (beta = 1.5) final lamina height/width aspect ratio = 1.1696 height/width [aspect_ratio(grow_stromatolite(v=1.5, lam=1.0)[-1])]; sharp cone regime (beta = 5.0) final lamina height/width aspect ratio = 2.6191 height/width [aspect_ratio(grow_stromatolite(v=5.0, lam=1.0)[-1])] — monotonic aspect-ratio progression across beta=(0.3, 1.5, 5.0): 0.669 < 1.170 < 2.619." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-4> ;
    pk:hasProbability 2.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — MorphoEval overall 43.6/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "`2010-petroff-stromatolite.py` implements Petroff et al.'s (2010) diffusion-competition spacing formula `ell = alpha * sqrt(D * tau)` (`ell = 0.66 cm` at `tau = 12 h`, `D = 1e-5 cm^2/s`, `alpha = 1.0`), renders a hexagonal packing diagram, and sweeps `beta = v/lambda` across `{0.3, 1.5, 5.0}` (and `0.2 -> 6.0` in the 70-frame GIF) to illustrate the transition from squat domes (`H/W = 0.67`) to tall cones (`H/W = 2.62`). However, the lamina growth model is not Petroff et al.'s diffusive-flux solver (`nabla^2 c = 0` with growth proportional to normal flux `dc/dn`), nor is it an exact integration of the Batchelor et al. (2004) KPZ equation printed in the docstring: it advances a pinned-base Lagrangian front with an unsourced quadratic crest-weighting `w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z_max)^2` and 3-point smoothing, and compares against no empirical stromatolite thin sections or measured spacing distributions. Overall 43.6/100 (faithfulness 37.2, reproducibility 58.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 5564750; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 44, Morphological realism / specimen match 30, Parameter expressivity 60, Morphometric validation 25, Source and data traceability 52, Code-to-model traceability 50, Reproducibility package 70. Output judged: petroff_stromatolite_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py at 5564750, image/png, 328721 B, 1736×1244 px, artifact_sha256 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01 (sha256 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01), spec_fingerprint 2b3289aae8f3466486ffbc5f503dd7585e6e1c2863ac78c108d1488932cf713f. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2b3289aae8f3466486ffbc5f503dd7585e6e1c2863ac78c108d1488932cf713f; artifact_sha256: 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Petroff et al. (2010): nutrient diffusion over active photosynthetic period tau sets inter-cone spacing ell = alpha * sqrt(D * tau) (~1 cm for daily cycle), and diffusive flux gradients along the mat interface govern lamina accretion and conical geometry | Batchelor et al. (2004): deterministic KPZ / normal-plus-vertical lamina accretion dh/dt = v + lambda * (1 + 1/2 (dh/dr)^2) transitions from domes to cones as beta = v / lambda increases; reconstructed_in_script: Algebraic diffusion-length spacing law ell = alpha * sqrt(D * tau) for alpha in {1.0, 0.30}, hexagonal close-packed cone lattice, and a 2D Lagrangian polyline front advancing by lambda * n_hat + v * w_photic * z_hat with pinned basal endpoints and 3-point Laplacian smoothing; transfer_boundary: The dome-to-cone lamina solver does not solve Petroff et al.'s Laplace diffusion equation (nabla^2 c = 0) or local diffusive flux; it substitutes a modified Batchelor et al. (2004) kinematic front with an ad-hoc photic weighting w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z_max)^2; does_not_claim: Direct comparison to digitized Yellowstone mat or Proterozoic Conophyton thin-section photographs or empirical cone-spacing histograms." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py:126-143,238-239 Document or remove the ad-hoc photic weighting `w_photic = 0.12 + 0.88*(z/z.max())**2`, release or widen the pinned basal footprint for the dome regime (`beta = 0.3`), and reconcile the `tau = 12 h` calculation (`ell = 0.66 cm`) with the `~20 h` text annotation.",
        "remediation needed: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py:86-163 Implement Petroff et al.'s (2010) steady-state nutrient diffusion field (nabla^2 c = 0 around periodic absorbing cones with normal velocity proportional to local diffusive flux dc/dn), and clearly separate it from the Batchelor et al. (2004) KPZ / Lagrangian front model.",
        "remediation needed: Create `datasets/petroff/` with a SHA-256-pinned transcription of Petroff et al.'s measured modern, lab, and fossil cone spacings plus a segmented *Conophyton* thin-section profile, and add `--self-test` and CSV metrics export." ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.36e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — Parameter expressivity: 60/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Sweeps daylight span `tau` continuously across `1..48 h` for two `alpha` regimes (`1.0` and `0.30`, L187-192), compares three `beta = v/lambda` regimes (`0.3, 1.5, 5.0`, L249-253) in the static figure, and sweeps `beta` logarithmically across 36 values (`0.2 -> 6.0`, L306) in `make_gif`, producing a strictly monotonic increase in height/width aspect ratio (`0.631 -> 3.030`). Deduct 25 points because no model parameters (`beta`, `D`, `alpha`, `smooth`, `seed_height`) are exposed on the CLI (L336-348), and 15 points because `lambda = 1.0`, `base_half = 1.0`, and `smooth = 0.03` are held fixed. Evidence: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L249–L273: 3 beta regimes (0.3, 1.5, 5.0) plotted on shared vertical scale <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L249-L273>; 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L300–L334: make_gif sweeps 36 log-spaced beta values from 0.2 to 6.0 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L300-L334>; 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L336–L348: CLI exposes only -o/--output, --gif, and --no-show <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L336-L348>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — Reproducibility package: 70/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The script is purely deterministic (no RNG), runs in < 1 s using only `numpy`, `matplotlib`, and `Pillow` (all pinned in `requirements.txt` and `requirements.lock.txt`), and supports `-o/--output`, `--gif`, and `--no-show`. Deduct 12 points because there is no `--self-test` mode or CSV metrics export; deduct 10 points because the docstring usage block (L45-48) omits `--gif` and the default output path is the repo root rather than `docs/media/petroff_stromatolite_dome_to_cone.gif`; and deduct 8 points because `show=True` is the default when no `--no-show` flag is passed. Evidence: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L45–L48: docstring CLI examples omit --gif <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L45-L48>; 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L336–L348: argparse entrypoint with -o/--output, --gif, --no-show <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L336-L348>; requirements.lock.txt L1–L51: pinned Python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.10.7, pillow 12.0.0 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L51>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — Source and data traceability: 52/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Module docstring cites Petroff et al. (2010) with full author list, title, journal, volume, pages, and PMCID (`PMC2890478`, L5-8), and names Batchelor, Burne, Henry & Jackson (2004) and Fejes Tóth (1948). Deduct 20 points because neither the primary paper's DOI (`10.1073/pnas.1001978107`) nor full bibliographic details/DOIs for Batchelor et al. (2004) and Fejes Tóth (1948) are recorded in the script; deduct 18 points because no `datasets/petroff/` directory, `README.md`, or `paper_citations.bib` exists; and deduct 10 points because `alpha_lab = 0.30` (L180) and the Bakal Formation `10-20 cm` spacing note (L241-243) lack specific table/figure pointers. Evidence: 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L5–L8: Petroff et al. 2010 citation with PMC2890478 but no DOI string <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L5-L8>; 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L27–L35: short inline mentions of Fejes Toth 1948 and Batchelor et al. 2004 without venue or DOI <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L27-L35>; 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L179–L180: alpha_field = 1.0 and alpha_lab = 0.30 without table/figure citation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L179-L180>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 5.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-petroff-kahng-audit-petroff-stromatolite-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Petroff et al. (2010) Conical Stromatolite Spacing Law & Dome-to-Cone Morphospace — Morphological realism / specimen match: 30/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The three bottom panels (`beta = 0.3, 1.5, 5.0`) and 70-frame animation clearly show internal lamina stacking and axial-zone crest thickening as `beta` increases. However, (-30) no fossil *Conophyton* thin-section, modern Yellowstone microbial mat photograph, or digitized figure from Petroff et al. (2010) is shown or overlaid; (-15) pinning the basal feet at `x = +-1` (L136-137) while starting from a triangular seed (L153) causes the `beta = 0.3` dome (Panel d) to form a steep-walled flat-topped trapezoid with a central crease rather than a hemispheroidal domal stromatolite; and (-15) the `beta = 5.0` sharp cone sits atop a vertical cylinder base with a rounded tip rather than exhibiting straight conical flanks. Evidence: petroff_stromatolite_morphospace.png (generated output, not in repo): 6-panel summary figure; no specimen thin-section or field photo; panel (d) dome has vertical side walls and central seed kink — petroff_stromatolite_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py at 5564750, image/png, 328721 B, 1736×1244 px, artifact_sha256 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01 (sha256 8e00cc6fabe5cf24f1544cbc867b0f6e9501cf7099a7b3da7166a2bf8fd1be01), spec_fingerprint 2b3289aae8f3466486ffbc5f503dd7585e6e1c2863ac78c108d1488932cf713f; docs/media/petroff_stromatolite_dome_to_cone.gif (generated output, not in repo): 70-frame ping-pong animation sweeping beta = 0.2 -> 6.0 — docs/media/petroff_stromatolite_dome_to_cone.gif: rendered output of 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py at 5564750, image/gif, 920055 B, 560×416 px, 70 frames, artifact_sha256 b7f825720b31f42faa4f7424f916639a76f36dfd50a2025cb0706b4d9ea55514 (sha256 b7f825720b31f42faa4f7424f916639a76f36dfd50a2025cb0706b4d9ea55514), spec_fingerprint 2b3289aae8f3466486ffbc5f503dd7585e6e1c2863ac78c108d1488932cf713f; 2010-petroff-stromatolite.py L136–L155: triangular seed z0 and pinned endpoints x[0]=-base_half, x[-1]=base_half <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/5564750/2010-petroff-stromatolite.py#L136-L155>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-petroff-stromatolite-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 3e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "unfaithful" .

