<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Ermentrout & Cowan (1979) / Bressloff et al. (2001) Retino-Cortical Pullback Classification" ;
    dct:description "Maps V1 roll planforms onto Klüver's tunnel, funnel and spiral form constants; the cortical lattice orientation decides which retinal form constant is seen | Variables: r, θ: retinal polar coordinates; x, y: cortical coordinates (mm); α, β: cortical magnification constants; ε: foveal scale; w₀: foveal radius; (k_x, k_y): cortical planform wavevector" ;
    dct:source "Ermentrout & Cowan (1979) Biol. Cybern. 34:137; Bressloff et al. (2001) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 356:299 §2; Bressloff et al. (2002) Neural Comput. 14:473 Eq. 1.1 (α, β values from upstream params.rs, not the papers)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L129-L173,L982-L1013,L1097-L1118>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L507-L531> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def retino_cortical_phase (kx ky x y : Int) : Int := kx * x + ky * y
theorem ermentrout_cowan_tunnel_rings (kx x y y' : Int) :
    retino_cortical_phase kx 0 x y = retino_cortical_phase kx 0 x y' := by simp [retino_cortical_phase]
theorem ermentrout_cowan_funnel_rays (ky x x' y : Int) :
    retino_cortical_phase 0 ky x y = retino_cortical_phase 0 ky x' y := by simp [retino_cortical_phase]
theorem ermentrout_cowan_log_spiral (kx ky x x' y y' : Int) :
    retino_cortical_phase kx ky x y - retino_cortical_phase kx ky x' y' =
    kx * (x - x') + ky * (y - y') := by
  simp [retino_cortical_phase, Int.mul_sub]
  omega"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "x = (α/ε) ln(1 + ε r/w₀),  y = β r θ/(w₀ + ε r)  (far field ε r ≫ w₀: x ≈ (α/ε) ln(ε r/w₀), y ≈ (β/ε) θ);  phase(k_x, k_y) = k_x x + k_y y:  k_y = 0 → rings (tunnel),  k_x = 0 → rays (funnel),  else log-spiral θ = c − (k_x/k_y) ln r" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1137/23M1616686>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking Neural-Field Bifurcation & Log-Polar Retino-Cortical Geometry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.retino_cortical_phase" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.ermentrout_cowan_log_spiral" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001) Cubic Amplitude-Equation Roll/Lattice Stability Boundary" ;
    dct:description "Selects rolls vs rhombic, square or hexagonal lattices (Figs. 37–40); decides whether a hallucination is a single-family tunnel/spiral or a cobweb/honeycomb | Variables: A_i: squared mode amplitudes; λ: bifurcation parameter (distance past marginal stability); γ₀ = γ₃(0): self-coupling; γ₃(θ): cross-mode cubic coupling at wavevector angle θ (Eq. 5.15)" ;
    dct:source "Bressloff et al. (2001) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 356:299 §5 Eqs. 5.12–5.15, Figs. 37–40" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L672-L697,L765-L916>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L533-L561> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def amplitude_rhs (lam gamma0 gamma_theta a_self a_other : Int) : Int :=
  lam - gamma0 * a_self - 2 * gamma_theta * a_other
theorem bressloff_roll_fixed_point (gamma0 gamma_theta a : Int) :
    amplitude_rhs (gamma0 * a) gamma0 gamma_theta a 0 = 0 := by simp [amplitude_rhs]
theorem bressloff_roll_transverse_growth (gamma0 gamma_theta a : Int) :
    amplitude_rhs (gamma0 * a) gamma0 gamma_theta 0 a = (gamma0 - 2 * gamma_theta) * a := by
  simp [amplitude_rhs, Int.sub_mul]
theorem bressloff_roll_stable_iff (gamma0 gamma_theta : Int) :
    amplitude_rhs (gamma0 * 1) gamma0 gamma_theta 0 1 < 0 ↔ gamma0 < 2 * gamma_theta := by
  simp [amplitude_rhs]
  omega
theorem bressloff_fig38_roll_unstable :
    amplitude_rhs (3768 * 1) 3768 1869 0 1 = 30 := by decide"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "dA₁/dt = A₁ (λ − γ₀ A₁ − 2 γ₃(θ) A₂);  roll fixed point λ = γ₀ A₁;  transverse growth (γ₀ − 2γ₃(θ)) A₁;  roll stable ⇔ γ₀ < 2 γ₃(θ)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1137/23M1616686>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking Neural-Field Bifurcation & Log-Polar Retino-Cortical Geometry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.amplitude_rhs" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.bressloff_roll_stable_iff" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/bressloff-v1-form-constants-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011) Floquet Resonance Tongues (1:1 Harmonic vs 2:1 Period-Doubling)" ;
    dct:description "Separates flicker-induced stripe phosphenes (harmonic tongue) from period-doubled hexagonal phosphenes (subharmonic tongue) across (T, β) | Variables: μ: Floquet multiplier of the homogeneous flicker orbit; T: forcing period (ms); β: normalised wave number; n: number of elapsed forcing periods" ;
    dct:source "Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011) PLoS Comput. Biol. 7(9):e1002158 Fig. 8" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1708-L1724,L2091-L2137>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d6f3c94/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L563-L588> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def floquet_iterate (mu : Int) : Nat → Int
  | 0 => 1
  | n + 1 => mu * floquet_iterate mu n
theorem rule_2011_harmonic_returns_each_period (n : Nat) : floquet_iterate 1 n = 1
theorem rule_2011_period_doubling_even_odd (n : Nat) :
    floquet_iterate (-1) (2 * n) = 1 ∧ floquet_iterate (-1) (2 * n + 1) = -1"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "mode after n forcing periods = μⁿ;  μ = +1 (1:1 stripes) → μⁿ = 1;  μ = −1 (2:1 hexagons) → μ^{2n} = 1, μ^{2n+1} = −1" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1001/archopht.1991.01080060080030>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1007/BF00336965>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2000.0769>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1137/23M1616686>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1162/089976602317250861>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002158> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking Neural-Field Bifurcation & Log-Polar Retino-Cortical Geometry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.floquet_iterate" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.rule_2011_period_doubling_even_odd" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cervera-levin-mafe-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Cervera-Levin-Mafe (2021) Gap-Junction Coupled Membrane Potential ODE" ;
    dct:description "Models bioelectric pattern memory, bistable polarized vs. depolarized domains, and double-head (2H) vs. wild-type (1H) planarian regeneration attractors | Variables: V_i: transmembrane voltage of cell i; C_m: membrane capacitance; I_dep, I_hyp: inward/outward ion currents; G_{ij}: gap-junction conductance" ;
    dct:source "Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021) J. Phys. Chem. B / Bioelectrochemistry" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L65-L185>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L229-L237> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gap_junction_current (G_ij V_i V_j : Int) : Int := G_ij * (V_j - V_i)
theorem cervera_equipotential_zero_current (G_ij V : Int) :
    gap_junction_current G_ij V V = 0 := by
  simp [gap_junction_current]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "C_m dV_i/dt = -I_dep(V_i) - I_hyp(V_i) + ∑_{j ∈ N(i)} G_{ij}(V_i, V_j) (V_j - V_i)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bioelechem.2019.107410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biosystems.2021.104511>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpj.2019.01.029>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.12.012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btt088> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Bioelectric Gap-Junction Coupled Nonlinear Dynamical Network" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.gap_junction_current" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.cervera_equipotential_zero_current" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/cervera-levin-mafe-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Voltage-Gated Bell-Boltzmann Gap-Junction Conductance" ;
    dct:description "Nonlinear intercellular coupling that isolates depolarized wounds or unlocks regional tissue-level bioelectric synchronization | Variables: G_0: maximum open gap-junction conductance; V_th: gating threshold voltage; V_0: thermal/voltage slope factor" ;
    dct:source "Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2021)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/2021-Cervera–Levin–Mafe.py#L110-L160>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/a0d6848/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L239-L248> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def bell_boltzmann_denom (b_i b_j : Nat) : Nat := (1 + b_i) * (1 + b_j)
theorem cervera_bell_boltzmann_symmetric (b_i b_j : Nat) :
    bell_boltzmann_denom b_i b_j = bell_boltzmann_denom b_j b_i := by
  simp [bell_boltzmann_denom, Nat.mul_comm]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "G_{ij}(V_i, V_j) = G_0 / [ (1 + exp((V_i - V_th)/V_0)) (1 + exp((V_j - V_th)/V_0)) ]" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bioelechem.2019.107410>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.biosystems.2021.104511>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpj.2019.01.029>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2009.12.012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btt088> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Bioelectric Gap-Junction Coupled Nonlinear Dynamical Network" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.bell_boltzmann_denom" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.cervera_bell_boltzmann_symmetric" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/chindapol-coral-flow-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Advection-Diffusion Nutrient Boundary Layer & Péclet Number" ;
    dct:description "Couples unidirectional vs. high-flow hydrodynamic boundary layer thinning to symmetric bushy vs. upstream-curved Pocillopora coral branching | Variables: c(x): dissolved inorganic carbon/nutrient concentration; u(x): flow velocity field; Pe: Péclet number; v_n: normal skeletal accretion rate" ;
    dct:source "Chindapol et al. (2013) PLoS Comput. Biol. 9(1):e1002849" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f3fe478/2013-chindapol-coral-flow.py#L60-L190>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f3fe478/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L344-L352> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def peclet_numerator (U L : Nat) : Nat := U * L
theorem chindapol_zero_flow_diffusive (L : Nat) :
    peclet_numerator 0 L = 0 := by
  simp [peclet_numerator]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "u · ∇c = D ∇^2 c,   Pe = U L / D,   v_n = k_g (∇c · n)|_Γ" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002849> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Advection-Diffusion Nutrient Transport & Péclet-Number Accretion" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.peclet_numerator" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.chindapol_zero_flow_diffusive" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/eshghi-odonata-wing-cells-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Odonata Wing Cell Circularity & Second-Moment Eigenvalue Elongation" ;
    dct:description "Measures proximo-distal and anterior-posterior cell size, circularity, and elongation gradients across dragonfly (Anisoptera) and damselfly (Zygoptera) wings | Variables: A_i, P_i: wing cell polygon area and perimeter; Σ_i: 2×2 boundary/interior covariance matrix; λ_min, λ_max: principal eigenvalues" ;
    dct:source "Eshghi et al. (2026) Odonata Wing Venation Morphometrics" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/2026-eshghi-odonata-wing-cells.py#L70-L215>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fbbcaf6/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L327-L336> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def elongation_anisotropy_diff (lam_max lam_min : Nat) : Nat := lam_max - lam_min
theorem eshghi_isotropic_zero_elongation (lam : Nat) :
    elongation_anisotropy_diff lam lam = 0 := by
  simp [elongation_anisotropy_diff]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "C_i = 4π A_i / P_i^2,   E_i = 1 - √(λ_min(Σ_i) / λ_max(Σ_i))" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1721248115>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19899648> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Spatial Polygonal Morphometrics & Covariance Eigenvalue Elongation" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.elongation_anisotropy_diff" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.eshghi_isotropic_zero_elongation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hoffmann-wing-venation-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Wing Vein Polygonal Cell Area & Isoperimetric Circularity Law" ;
    dct:description "Quantifies primary vs. secondary insect wing venation domain geometry and cell shape distributions | Variables: (x_k, y_k): ordered polygon vertices of wing cell i; A_i: polygon area; P_i: perimeter; C_i: isoperimetric circularity" ;
    dct:source "Hoffmann, Donoughe et al. (2018) PNAS 115(40):9905-9910" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f3fe478/2018-hoffmann-wing-venation.py#L60-L180>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f3fe478/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L311-L319> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def shoelace_edge_term (xk yk xk1 yk1 : Int) : Int := xk * yk1 - xk1 * yk
theorem hoffmann_shoelace_antisymmetric (xk yk xk1 yk1 : Int) :
    shoelace_edge_term xk1 yk1 xk yk = - shoelace_edge_term xk yk xk1 yk1 := by
  simp [shoelace_edge_term, Int.neg_sub]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "A_i = (1/2) |∑_{k=1}^m (x_k y_{k+1} - x_{k+1} y_k)|,   C_i = 4π A_i / P_i^2 ∈ (0, 1]" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1721248115> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Planar Straight-Line Graph (PSLG) Polygonal Tessellation Geometry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.shoelace_edge_term" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.hoffmann_shoelace_antisymmetric" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/lobo-limbform-morphology-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Lobo et al. (2014) Limbform Recursive Segmental Tree Vector Law" ;
    dct:description "Decodes normal, regenerating, and ectopic/supernumerary amphibian and vertebrate limb morphologies from LimbformDB | Variables: L_k: limb podial/zeugopod/stylopod segment length; α_j: relative joint branching angle; r: segment radius" ;
    dct:source "Lobo, Feldman & Levin (2014) Dev. Biol. / Bioinformatics" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L75-L210>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L274-L287> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """inductive LimbTree where
  | leaf (length : Nat) : LimbTree
  | branch (length : Nat) (child : LimbTree) : LimbTree
theorem lobo_2014_three_segment_axis (L1 L2 L3 : Nat) :
    limb_segment_count (LimbTree.branch L1 (LimbTree.branch L2 (LimbTree.leaf L3))) = 3 := by rfl"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "x_{k+1} = x_k + L_k [cos(∑_{j≤k} α_j), sin(∑_{j≤k} α_j)]^T,   T = (s, α, r, L, children)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1002/reg2.13>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btu582> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Recursive Tree Graph Grammar & Segmental Kinematics" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.limb_segment_count" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.lobo_2014_three_segment_axis" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/planform-morphology-animation-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Lobo et al. (2013) PlanformDB Region-Link Polar Graph Encoding" ;
    dct:description "Decodes all 369 relational planarian body morphologies and internal organ placements (eyes, brain, pharynx) from PlanformDB | Variables: p_A, p_B: connected body-region centers; θ_{AB}: polar attachment angle; r_{ant}, r_{post}, r_{lat}: directional semi-axes" ;
    dct:source "Lobo, Malone & Levin (2013) PLoS Comput. Biol. 9(10):e1003287" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L80-L240>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L256-L266> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def planform_wildtype_ap_length (r_head r_ant_trunk r_post_trunk r_tail : Nat) : Nat :=
  r_head + r_ant_trunk + r_post_trunk + r_tail
theorem lobo_2013_wildtype_dimensions :
    planform_wildtype_ap_length 80 200 200 80 = 560 ∧ (60 + 60 : Nat) = 120 := by decide"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "p_B = p_A + r_A(θ_{AB}) u(θ_{AB}) + d_{AB} u(θ_{AB}),   R_i(φ) = piecewise-ellipse(r_{ant}, r_{post}, r_{lat})" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpj.2017.04.011>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btt088>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/bio.20123400> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Formal Anatomical Region Graph Grammar & Polar Geometry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.planform_wildtype_ap_length" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.lobo_2013_wildtype_dimensions" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/raup-shell-coiling-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Raup (1966) 4-Parameter Logarithmic Helicospiral Surface" ;
    dct:description "Spans gastropod, cephalopod, bivalve, and brachiopod shell morphospace in 3D cylindrical coordinates | Variables: W: whorl expansion rate; D: relative distance of generating curve from coiling axis; T: whorl translation rate (dz_c/dr_c); S: aperture aspect ratio" ;
    dct:source "Raup (1966) J. Paleontol. 40(5):1178-1190 Eq. (1)-(6); Noshita (2014)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/create_raup_animations.py#L72-L148>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L147-L169> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def raup_whorl_radius (r0 W : Nat) : Nat → Nat
  | 0 => r0
  | k + 1 => W * raup_whorl_radius r0 W k
theorem raup_whorl_expansion_recovery (r0 W k : Nat) :
    raup_whorl_radius r0 W (k + 1) = W * raup_whorl_radius r0 W k := by rfl"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "r(θ, φ) = r_0 W^{θ/2π} [1 + ((1 - D)/(1 + D)) cos φ],   z(θ, φ) = r_0 T (W^{θ/2π} - 1) + r_0 W^{θ/2π} S ((1 - D)/(1 + D)) sin φ" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2014.08.010>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/srep42445>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.138.3537.150>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.147.3663.1294>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2307/1301992> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Logarithmic Helicospiral Parametric Differential Geometry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.raup_whorl_radius" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.raup_whorl_expansion_recovery" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/raup-shell-coiling-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Generating-Curve Center Parameter Recovery Identities" ;
    dct:description "Exact inverse morphometric recovery verifying 3D mesh fidelity against input (W, D, T) across all 6 canonical shell regimes | Variables: r_c, z_c: generating-curve centroid coordinates; r_min, r_max: inner and outer aperture margins" ;
    dct:source "Raup (1966) J. Paleontol. 40(5):1178-1190; Okabe & Yoshimura (2017)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L161-L173>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/ba6fd20/morphoeval/measure_outputs.py#L220-L310> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def raup_axial_step (T delta_r : Nat) : Nat := T * delta_r
theorem raup_translation_rate_recovery (T delta_r : Nat) (h_pos : delta_r > 0) :
    (raup_axial_step T delta_r) / delta_r = T := by
  simp [raup_axial_step, Nat.mul_div_cancel _ h_pos]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "W_rec = r_c(θ) / r_c(θ - 2π),   D_rec = r_min(θ) / r_max(θ),   T_rec = Δz_c / Δr_c" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2014.08.010>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/srep42445>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.138.3537.150>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.147.3663.1294>,
        <https://doi.org/10.2307/1301992> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Logarithmic Helicospiral Parametric Differential Geometry" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.raup_axial_step" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.raup_translation_rate_recovery" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1926) / Price et al. (2013) Vascular Pipe-Model Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Governs basipetal vascular radius accumulation and daughter/parent cross-sectional area ratios across Horton-Strahler orders 1-8 | Variables: r_parent, r_i: parent and daughter vein radii; γ ∈ [2, 3]: vascular scaling exponent (γ = 3 Murray cube law in minor veins -> γ = 2 Da Vinci area-preserving in major veins)" ;
    dct:source "Murray (1926) PNAS 12:207; Runions et al. (2005) Sec. 3.5; Price, Knox & Brodribb (2013) PLoS ONE 8(12):e85420" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L463-L518>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L367-L403> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ObeysMurrayLaw (γ : Nat) : VeinTree → Prop
  | VeinTree.tip _ => True
  | VeinTree.fork r l right =>
      r ^ γ = (vein_root_radius l) ^ γ + (vein_root_radius right) ^ γ ∧
      ObeysMurrayLaw γ l ∧ ObeysMurrayLaw γ right
theorem murray_1926_tree_conservation (γ : Nat) (t : VeinTree) (h : ObeysMurrayLaw γ t) :
    (vein_root_radius t) ^ γ = sum_gamma_powers γ (vein_tip_radii t)"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "r_parent^γ = ∑_{i ∈ children} r_i^γ,   r_root^γ = ∑_{leaf ∈ tips} r_leaf^γ" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004680>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0037994>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0085420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Auxin Space-Colonization, Murray's Minimum-Work Vascular Law & Planar Dual Loop Nesting" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.ObeysMurrayLaw" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.murray_1926_tree_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Runions et al. (2005) Eq. (2)-(3) Toussaint Relative Neighborhood Graph (RNG) Lune Law" ;
    dct:description "Attracts multiple surrounding vein tips toward a shared auxin source via empty-lune RNG neighborhoods to form closed anastomosing areole loops | Variables: s ∈ S: discrete auxin source; v ∈ V: vein node; V(s): Relative Neighborhood vein set; D: vein advance step; d_k: kill distance" ;
    dct:source "Runions, Fuhrer, Lane, Federl, Rolland-Lagan & Prusinkiewicz (2005) ACM Trans. Graph. 24(3):702-711 Eq. (1)-(3)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L183-L456>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L410-L422> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def in_rng_lune (d_vs d_us d_vu : Nat) : Prop := d_us < d_vs ∧ d_vu < d_vs
def rng_witness_excludes (d_vs d_us d_vu : Nat) : Bool := Nat.max d_us d_vu < d_vs
theorem runions_2005_rng_lune_iff (d_vs d_us d_vu : Nat) :
    rng_witness_excludes d_vs d_us d_vu = true ↔ in_rng_lune d_vs d_us d_vu := by
  simp [rng_witness_excludes, in_rng_lune, Nat.max_lt]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "V(s) = {v ∈ V : ∀ u ∈ V, ||v - s|| ≤ max(||u - s||, ||v - u||)},   v' = v + D (∑_{s ∈ S(v)} (s - v)/||s - v||) / ||∑_{s ∈ S(v)} (s - v)/||s - v||||" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004680>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0037994>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0085420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Auxin Space-Colonization, Murray's Minimum-Work Vascular Law & Planar Dual Loop Nesting" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.rng_witness_excludes" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.runions_2005_rng_lune_iff" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/runions-leaf-venation-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Euler-Poincaré Planar Areole Cycle Rank & Katifori (2012) Hierarchical Edge-Deletion Law" ;
    dct:description "Separates open dichotomous venation (L = 0, e.g. Ginkgo biloba) from closed reticulate venation (L > 0) and quantifies hierarchical loop nesting | Variables: V, E: planar vascular vertices and edges; L: enclosed areole count; r_j, s_j: merged subtree sizes in hierarchical loop decomposition; i_u: unweighted nesting number" ;
    dct:source "Katifori & Magnasco (2012) PLoS ONE 7(6):e37994; Ronellenfitsch et al. (2015) PLoS Comput. Biol. 11(12):e1004680" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/2005-runions-leaf-venation.py#L634-L712>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L430-L444> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def planar_cycle_count (edges vertices : Nat) : Nat := edges + 1 - vertices
theorem katifori_2012_tree_zero_cycles (n_edges : Nat) :
    planar_cycle_count n_edges (n_edges + 1) = 0 := by simp [planar_cycle_count]
theorem katifori_2012_edge_deletion_merges_areoles (n_edges k_bridges : Nat) (h : 1 ≤ k_bridges) :
    planar_cycle_count (n_edges + k_bridges - 1) (n_edges + 1) =
    planar_cycle_count (n_edges + k_bridges) (n_edges + 1) - 1"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "L = E - V + 1,   q_j = 1 - |r_j - s_j| / (r_j + s_j - 1),   i_u = (1/(N-1)) ∑_j q_j" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.12.3.207>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1145/1073204.1073251>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1004680>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0037994>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0085420> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Auxin Space-Colonization, Murray's Minimum-Work Vascular Law & Planar Dual Loop Nesting" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.planar_cycle_count" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.katifori_2012_edge_deletion_merges_areoles" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/santella-wormguides-celegans-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Sulston Embryonic Binary Lineage Division & 4D Nuclear Interpolation" ;
    dct:description "Reconstructs 3D embryonic morphogenesis, gastrulation, and ventral enclosure of Caenorhabditis elegans from WormGUIDES nuclear tracks | Variables: x_i(t) = (X_i, Y_i, Z_i): 3D nuclear centroid of blastomere i at embryonic minute t; founder lineages ∈ {AB, MS, E, C, D, P4}" ;
    dct:source "Santella et al. (2015) BMC Bioinformatics 16:189; Sulston et al. (1983)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/2015-santella-wormguides-celegans.py#L90-L230>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/303a87e/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L295-L303> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def nuclear_lerp (x0 x1 lam : Int) : Int := (1 - lam) * x0 + lam * x1
theorem sulston_nuclear_lerp_endpoints (x0 x1 : Int) :
    nuclear_lerp x0 x1 0 = x0 ∧ nuclear_lerp x0 x1 1 = x1 := by
  simp [nuclear_lerp]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "x_i(t) = (1 - λ(t)) x_i(t_k) + λ(t) x_i(t_{k+1}),   v_i(t) = ||x_i(t + Δt) - x_i(t)|| / Δt" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0012-1606(83)90201-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-019-1352-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1083/jcb.144.5.927>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2017.0382>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1186/s12859-015-0627-8> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Sulston Binary Lineage Tree & 4D Spatiotemporal Trajectory Kinematics" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.nuclear_lerp" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.sulston_nuclear_lerp_endpoints" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "2D Biharmonic Thin-Plate Spline (TPS) Deformation Field" ;
    dct:description "Maps homologous anatomical landmarks of Scarus (parrotfish) onto Pomacanthus (angelfish) with minimum bending energy | Variables: (x, y): source Scarus landmark coordinates; r_i = ||(x,y) - p_i||; w_i: biharmonic kernel weights" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) On Growth and Form Ch. XVII Fig. 517-518; Bookstein (1989) IEEE TPAMI 11:567" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L181-L189>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson.py#L95-L185> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def tps_zero_displacement_kernel (r_sq log_r_sq : Int) : Int := r_sq * log_r_sq
theorem tps_kernel_zero_at_origin (log_val : Int) :
    tps_zero_displacement_kernel 0 log_val = 0 := by
  simp [tps_zero_displacement_kernel]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Φ(x, y) = a_0 + a_x x + a_y y + ∑_{i=1}^K w_i r_i^2 ln(r_i^2),  Δ^2 Φ = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-93093-5>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.24792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/evo.13755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0112732>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.fn457gr> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Biharmonic Thin-Plate Spline & Affine Coordinate Transformation" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.tps_zero_displacement_kernel" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.tps_kernel_zero_at_origin" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/thompson-scarus-pomacanthus-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Affine Oblique Shear & Principal Strain Tensor" ;
    dct:description "Linear global coordinate shear baseline compared against non-affine TPS warp across 14 anatomical landmarks | Variables: α_x, α_y: axial stretch ratios; γ_xy, γ_yx: oblique grid shear angles; J: local areal dilation" ;
    dct:source "Thompson (1917) On Growth and Form Ch. XVII" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L191-L200>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/232e8f8/thompson/1917-thompson.py#L186-L260> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def affine_jacobian_det (a_x a_y g_xy g_yx : Int) : Int := a_x * a_y - g_xy * g_yx
theorem thompson_unit_shear_area_preserving (g_xy : Int) :
    affine_jacobian_det 1 1 g_xy 0 = 1 := by
  simp [affine_jacobian_det]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "x' = α_x x + γ_xy y + t_x,  y' = γ_yx x + α_y y + t_y;  J = det(∇Φ)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-93093-5>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1109/34.24792>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1111/evo.13755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0112732>,
        <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.fn457gr> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Biharmonic Thin-Plate Spline & Affine Coordinate Transformation" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.affine_jacobian_det" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.thompson_unit_shear_area_preserving" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/turing-gray-scott-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Gray-Scott Autocatalytic Reaction-Diffusion System" ;
    dct:description "Generates symmetry-breaking Turing spots (mitosis), labyrinthine stripes, and coral/soliton regimes across (F, k) morphospace | Variables: u(x,y,t): substrate concentration; v(x,y,t): autocatalyst concentration; D_u, D_v: diffusivities; F: feed rate; k: kill rate" ;
    dct:source "Turing (1952) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 237:37; Pearson (1993) Science 261:189" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f3fe478/1952-turing-morpho.py#L45-L140>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/f3fe478/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L208-L221> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def gray_scott_react_u (F u v : Int) : Int := -(u * v * v) + F * (1 - u)
def gray_scott_react_v (F k u v : Int) : Int := u * v * v - (F + k) * v
theorem gray_scott_homogeneous_equilibrium (F k : Int) :
    gray_scott_react_u F 1 0 = 0 ∧ gray_scott_react_v F k 1 0 = 0 := by
  simp [gray_scott_react_u, gray_scott_react_v]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "∂u/∂t = D_u ∇^2 u - u v^2 + F(1 - u),   ∂v/∂t = D_v ∇^2 v + u v^2 - (F + k)v" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.261.5118.189> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Reaction-Diffusion Partial Differential Equations (PDE)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.gray_scott_react_u" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.gray_scott_homogeneous_equilibrium" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/vogel-phyllotaxis-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Vogel (1979) Planar Capitulum Golden-Angle Spiral Law" ;
    dct:description "Constant-area centripetal floret packing producing the rising Fibonacci parastichy cascade (8,13)->(13,21)->(21,34)->(34,55) and bounded Voronoi optimality | Variables: n: floret plastochron index; r_n: radial distance; θ_n: divergence angle; τ = (1+√5)/2: golden ratio; J: jugacy" ;
    dct:source "Vogel (1979) Mathematical Biosciences 44:179-189 Eq. (1)-(4)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L110-L154>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L97-L116> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def vogel_radius_sq (c_sq n : Nat) : Nat := c_sq * n
theorem vogel_constant_annulus_area (c_sq n : Nat) :
    vogel_radius_sq c_sq (n + 1) - vogel_radius_sq c_sq n = c_sq := by
  simp [vogel_radius_sq, Nat.mul_add, Nat.add_sub_cancel_left]
theorem vogel_fibonacci_parastichy_cascade :
    (fib 6, fib 7) = (8, 13) ∧ (fib 7, fib 8) = (13, 21) ∧ (fib 8, fib 9) = (21, 34) ∧
    (fib 9, fib 10) = (34, 55) ∧ (fib 10, fib 11) = (55, 89) := by decide"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "r_n = c √n,   θ_n = n α_0 (mod 2π),   α_0 = 360° / τ^2 = 360° (2 - τ) ≈ 137.507764°" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0024>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0025-5564(79)90080-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.160091>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Kinematic Spiral Geometry, Repulsive Dynamical Systems & Delaunay Topology" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.vogel_radius_sq" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.vogel_constant_annulus_area" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/vogel-phyllotaxis-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Douady & Couder (1992, 1996) Hofmeister Inhibitory Energy Minimization" ;
    dct:description "Dynamical self-organization of sequentially initiated primordia onto the main Fibonacci (137.51°) and Lucas (99.50°) noble-angle attractors | Variables: G = v Δt / r_0: dimensionless plastochron ratio; λ: inhibitory interaction decay length; d(·): Euclidean distance on meristem" ;
    dct:source "Douady & Couder (1992) Phys. Rev. Lett. 68:2098; (1996) J. Theor. Biol. 178:255" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L383-L441>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L118-L128> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def hofmeister_pair_kernel (kernel_fn : Nat → Nat) (dist_sq : Nat) : Nat := kernel_fn dist_sq
theorem douady_couder_kernel_symmetric (kernel_fn : Nat → Nat) (d_ij d_ji : Nat)
    (h_sym : d_ij = d_ji) :
    hofmeister_pair_kernel kernel_fn d_ij = hofmeister_pair_kernel kernel_fn d_ji := by
  rw [h_sym]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "E(θ) = ∑_{j < n} exp(-d(r_0, θ; r_j(t), θ_j) / λ),   θ_n^* = argmin_θ E(θ),   r_j(t) = r_0 (1 + G)^m" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0024>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0025-5564(79)90080-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.160091>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Kinematic Spiral Geometry, Repulsive Dynamical Systems & Delaunay Topology" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.hofmeister_pair_kernel" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.douady_couder_kernel_symmetric" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/vogel-phyllotaxis-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Delaunay Contact Parastichy & Outer-Rim Dislocation Asymmetry" ;
    dct:description "Explains why incomplete outer-rim contact chains under biological noise cause a 3:1 excess of (Fibonacci - 1) over (Fibonacci + 1) counts in Swinton et al. (2016) | Variables: (m, n): opposed Delaunay contact-spiral counts in annulus [r_1, r_2); σ_r, σ_θ: biological placement noise" ;
    dct:source "Swinton, Ochu & MSI Turing's Sunflower Consortium (2016) R. Soc. Open Sci. 3:160091 Table 1" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/1979-vogel-phyllotaxis.py#L470-L562>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/c89d18d/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L130-L139> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def rim_dislocation_count (m_fib : Nat) (lost_chain : Bool) : Nat :=
  if lost_chain then m_fib - 1 else m_fib
theorem swinton_rim_dislocation_nonincreasing (m_fib : Nat) (lost_chain : Bool) :
    rim_dislocation_count m_fib lost_chain ≤ m_fib := by
  cases lost_chain <;> simp [rim_dislocation_count, Nat.sub_le]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "m_obs = m_Fib - Δm_rim (Δm_rim ∈ {0, 1}),   P(Fib - 1) > P(Fib + 1)  (binomial p = 5.07×10^{-5})" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1006/jtbi.1996.0024>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0025-5564(79)90080-4>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsos.160091>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Kinematic Spiral Geometry, Repulsive Dynamical Systems & Delaunay Topology" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.rim_dislocation_count" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.swinton_rim_dislocation_nonincreasing" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Wolfram (1983, 1984) Rule 30 Boolean & GF(2) Algebraic Normal Form" ;
    dct:description "Discrete chaotic generator of self-similar white triangular tents on Conus textile shells and OEIS A051023 center column | Variables: a_{t,i} ∈ {0, 1}: pigment state at mantle cell i and step t; ⊕: XOR; ∨: OR" ;
    dct:source "Wolfram (1983) Rev. Mod. Phys. 55:601; (1984) Nature 311:419" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L96-L152>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L21-L37> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def rule30 (p q r : Bool) : Bool := bne p (q || r)
def rule30_anf (p q r : Bool) : Bool := bne (bne p q) (bne r (q && r))
theorem rule30_anf_equiv (p q r : Bool) : rule30 p q r = rule30_anf p q r := by
  cases p <;> cases q <;> cases r <;> rfl"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "a_{t+1, i} = a_{t, i-1} ⊕ (a_{t, i} ∨ a_{t, i+1}) ≡ a_{t, i-1} + a_{t, i} + a_{t, i+1} + a_{t, i} a_{t, i+1} (mod 2)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0167-2789(90)90169-P>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(87)80101-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/311419a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.55.601> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Elementary Cellular Automata (GF(2)) & Reaction-Diffusion PDE" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.rule30" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.rule30_anf_equiv" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Erica Jen (1990) Left-Bijective Spatial Inverse & Diagonal Period-Doubling Recursion" ;
    dct:description "Proves exact left-bijectivity (0 bit errors) and explains why left-cone diagonals lock into period-doubling crystals separated by d_{k-1}=0 barriers | Variables: d_k(t) = a_{t, k-t}: k-th left-cone diagonal; P_k = 2^m: exact temporal period doubling at k ∈ {0, 3, 8, 29, 400, ...}" ;
    dct:source "Jen (1990) Physica D 45(1-3):3-18 Theorem 1 & Section 2" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L172-L256>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L39-L61> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def rule30_left_inverse (a_next q r : Bool) : Bool := bne a_next (q || r)
theorem jen_1990_left_bijective (p q r : Bool) :
    rule30_left_inverse (rule30 p q r) q r = p := by
  cases p <;> cases q <;> cases r <;> rfl
theorem jen_1990_barrier_shielding (d_km2 d_k : Bool) :
    jen_diagonal_step d_km2 true d_k = !d_km2 := by
  cases d_km2 <;> cases d_k <;> rfl"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "a_{t, i-1} = a_{t+1, i} ⊕ (a_{t, i} ∨ a_{t, i+1}),   d_k(t+1) = d_{k-2}(t) ⊕ (d_{k-1}(t) ∨ d_k(t))" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0167-2789(90)90169-P>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(87)80101-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/311419a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.55.601> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Elementary Cellular Automata (GF(2)) & Reaction-Diffusion PDE" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.rule30_left_inverse" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.jen_1990_left_bijective" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Meinhardt & Klingler (1987) 3-Species Activator-Substrate-Hormone Mantle PDE" ;
    dct:description "Continuous biochemical mechanism producing self-extinguishing pigment triangles and V-shaped travelling waves after mantle lesion | Variables: a(x,t): pigment activator; s(x,t): depleted substrate; h(x,t): fast-diffusing systemic hormone" ;
    dct:source "Meinhardt & Klingler (1987) J. Theor. Biol. 126(1):63-89 Eq. (1)-(3)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L315-L412>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/morphoeval/lean/MathOfBiology.lean#L63-L82> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def meinhardt_activator_reaction (rho kappa rho0 mu_a : Nat) (a s : Nat) : Int :=
  Int.ofNat (rho * s * (a * a + rho0 * (1 + kappa * a * a))) -
    Int.ofNat (mu_a * a * (1 + kappa * a * a))
theorem meinhardt_basal_quiescence (rho kappa mu_a s : Nat) :
    meinhardt_activator_reaction rho kappa 0 mu_a 0 s = 0 := by
  simp [meinhardt_activator_reaction]"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "∂a/∂t = ρ s (a^2 / (1 + κ a^2) + ρ_0) - μ_a a + D_a ∂^2a/∂x^2,   ∂s/∂t = σ (h / (1 + γ h)) - ρ s a^2 - μ_s s + D_s ∂^2s/∂x^2" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/0167-2789(90)90169-P>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-5193(87)80101-7>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/311419a0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/RevModPhys.55.601> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Elementary Cellular Automata (GF(2)) & Reaction-Diffusion PDE" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.meinhardt_activator_reaction" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.meinhardt_basal_quiescence" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

